(41007,	1997,	256,	'Stability\r\n\r\nIsaiah 28:16 says, Therefore thus saith the Lord God, Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious corner stone, a sure foundation: he that believeth shall not make haste. \r\n\r\nWhen we are firmly founded in the Word of God, we will not easily panic when trials come our way. Having faith in His Word will give stability and peace.\r\nRevealed Knowledge vs. Sense Knowledge\r\n\r\nWhen we just hear and read the Word of God without any revelation, it becomes short-lived. We tend to forget what we heard and saw. Unlike the revealed knowledge, it causes amazement in us. It firmly stick with us till we die. This kind of knowledge helps us to become firmly founded and stable in God\'s Word which leads us to avoid being snared by the enemy\'s trap.\r\nPeter\'s Response in John 6:67-69\r\n\r\nThen said Jesus unto the twelve, Will ye also go away? Then Simon Peter answered him, Lord, to whom shall we go? thou hast the words of eternal life. And we believe and are sure that thou art that Christ, the Son of the living God.\r\n\r\nJesus was intentionally offensive when he said to the Jewish crowd to eat his flesh and drink his blood. They readily walked out on Him in spite of witnessing all the signs and wonders that Jesus had done before their very eyes. Yet, when Jesus asked his true disciples if they will follow the crowd that left, Peter even when he did not understand Jesus\' offensive statement stayed not because of what the Lord had done but because of the revealed knowledge he had of who really Jesus is.',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11'),
(41008,	1997,	257,	'To ask God to give a fresh revelation of who He is and what His will is every time I read His Word.',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11'),
(41009,	1997,	258,	'We ought not measure the spirituality of a brother/sister by the gifts, talents and position they are holding in the ministry or even his or her tenure in the church. \r\n\r\nSpiritual growth is measured on how one exercises the fruit of the spirit in one\'s life consistently. However, spiritual growth is attained by undergoing trials. The question is are we willing to go through the painful process just so we can be like Christ?',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11',	'2017-10-05 12:15:11'),
(41010,	374,	8216,	'miracle\r\nmagic\r\nthe one whose does miracles',	'2017-10-04 14:55:50',	'2017-10-04 14:55:50'),
