(41013,	1194,	91,	'We should have a willing and submitted attitude in our obedience.\r\nGod will bless those who don\'t obey their authority when they are told to sin.\r\nYou are walking in the life that God called you to walk when the outside unbelievers cannot find fault in your life.',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36'),
(41014,	1194,	92,	'Whenever my authority tells me to do something against the word of God, I will still speak to them in a respectful manner.',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36'),
(41015,	1194,	93,	'Most people only submit to their authorities if it\'s something they agree with but real submission begins when they submit even though they disagree.',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36',	'2017-10-04 15:16:36'),
(41016,	374,	8231,	'who is going to be on God side\r\nPlaces of honour\r\nWho has more Faith',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11'),
(41017,	374,	8232,	'who is going to be on God side\r\nPlaces of honour\r\nWho has more Faith',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11'),
(41018,	374,	8233,	'Spreading the Gospel',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11'),
(41019,	374,	8234,	'Nil',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11',	'2017-10-04 15:31:11'),
(41020,	2008,	211,	'Anything that you go through, God will use it as a stepping stone of your life if you respond with obedience.\r\nOften the thing that looks like an abortion of God’s plan actually ends up being the road to its fulfillment if we stay in obedience and free from offense.\r\nIt is one thing for us to pursue God. It is another thing to have God pursuing us.',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24'),
(41021,	2008,	212,	'Through every trial, I will trust God\'s plan and have faith that God is using my situation to lead me to the fulfillment of His will in my life.',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24'),
(41022,	2008,	213,	'I have been under leaders that caused so much pain and discouragement in my walk with God. But as I look back now, this phase  in my life had taught me to become more obedient to God\'s words and helped me to become more patient, more understanding and more submissive to people in authority.',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24',	'2017-10-05 10:10:24'),
(41023,	2008,	226,	'A lot of people miss what God is continuing to say by stopping at the end of the chapter and then the next day picking up with the beginning of the next.\r\nAll authorities are appointed by God.\r\nWhen people are offended, they become a spiritual vagabond because of a persecution complex.',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07'),
(41024,	2008,	227,	'All authorities are appointed by God, therefore we have to pay respect for those whom we are under authority. If we find something that we feel that is not right with them, lay it down to God in prayer.',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07'),
(41025,	2008,	228,	'We have to be careful with letting offense take over our lives. It has more consequences than what we simply think of. Let go of the offense and let God take care of your situation. He knows, He guides, He is making a way for you, trust Him.',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07',	'2017-10-31 16:02:07'),
(41026,	1997,	271,	'Luke 22:21-24\r\nAnd they began to enquire among themselves, which of them it was that should do this thing.\r\n\r\nThis verse looks harmless not until you read the following verse. \r\n\r\nLuke 22:24\r\nAnd there was also a strife among them, which of them should be accounted the greatest.\r\n\r\nI wasn\'t able to see this in this light until now. Instead of being concerned with Jesus on who\'s going to betray the Lord, the disciples argued among themselves about their achievements with their relationship with Jesus. So, the one who has weightier knowledge and relationship with the Lord is less likely to betray Him. Wrong.\r\n\r\nNo wonder, Peter was asked by the enemy to be sifted so that his pride would be removed from his spirit. \r\n\r\nJesus did not intervene in the process of Peter\'s sifting for He knew Peter better than Peter himself. Instead, the Lord prayed for him that whatever faith he had on the revealed knowledge of Jesus Christ would keep him from failing. And when he recovered from the sifting process, he can now strengthen his brethren. \r\n\r\nLuke 22:32\r\nBut I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren.\r\n\r\nCome to think of it, we are still being strengthened by Peter\'s letters.\r\nStrong Souls vs. Strong Spirit\r\n\r\nStrong souls relates to how the flesh reacts to trials and sufferings, thru pressures unwisely. While a strong spirit is about how we submit to the will of God and act wisely in spite of the pressure at hand.\r\nPeter, lovest thou me?\r\n\r\nPeter answered Jesus yes. However, the kind of love Peter understands is that love brought about by the strong soul in him which is the Phileo love and not the Agape love that only comes from the Spirit of God. Nevertheless, Jesus entrusted to Peter the feeding of his sheep.',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46'),
(41027,	1997,	272,	'I can relate to Peter\'s strong soul because the pride in him is also in me. I will study Peter\'s letters and ask God to give me fresh revelations of His word.',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46'),
(41028,	1997,	273,	'Peter\r\n\r\nI thank God for His testimonies in the life of Peter. If Peter cowered and quit, I wouldn\'t have the privilege to read and learn from his writings and experiences. \r\n\r\nAll the glory to Jesus!',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46',	'2017-10-06 08:45:46'),
