(41098,	4015,	1171,	'If you get in a pattern of doing what is right then you won\'t lose what you labored for\r\nAll true honor is a result from the fear of the Lord.\r\nAll true honor originates from the heart.',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48'),
(41099,	4015,	1172,	'Not to complain to God about my circumstances.',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48'),
(41100,	4015,	1173,	'There are full rewards, partially rewards, and no rewards on earth and in heaven and hell',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48',	'2017-10-06 06:28:48'),
(41101,	1194,	106,	'The person\'s that is in authority over you heart is in the hand of the Lord and He can turn it any way He desires, whether you like it or not.\r\nIf we are able to do the most difficult task God asked us to do, that means we\'ll do anything.\r\nIshmael is what Abraham birthed from the flesh, God wanted Abraham to sacrifice his promised son who was Isaac.',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27'),
(41102,	1194,	107,	'If my authority tells me to cancel that I\'ve been working on for so long or what God told me to do, I\'ll do it because God wants to test me to see if I\'ll submit to His delegated authority and if I\'m willing to give up my Isaac.',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27'),
(41103,	1194,	108,	'Nobody can get you out of the call of God in your life, not even a leader, only you can. If we are complaining about our circumstances, we are not complaining towards our leaders but to God. I want to be like Esther and David who still spoke with respect to their leaders even though they didn\'t have all the information. The leaders saw their faith in God through the way they spoke. There will be times when God will test me to see if I\'ll actually do it, even though it doesn\'t make sense. There was one time when my mother told me not to go for this church training program which was meant for only some people but I thought it was something God wanted me to do but I still chose to submit to her and not attend the program. Because of that, I managed to do really well for my examinations and to me, that little thing that I \"gave up\" was my Isaac and I managed to get even more training after that so I believe when I do submit to my authorities , God will come through for me and will bless me.',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27',	'2017-10-06 07:44:27'),
(41104,	1997,	286,	'True meaning of Believe\r\n\r\nIn the Bible, the true meaning of \"Believe\" can be seen in Hebrews 3:12-19. It means that to believe is to OBEY. However, in today\'s time the term has degenerated. Acknowledging truth without complying is enough.\r\n\r\nIn Mark 16:16 which says, He that believeth and is baptized shall be saved; but he that believeth not shall be damned. Here, other denominations will emphasize that one just has to believe without the need to get baptized for the said reason above.\r\n\r\nNow, through this wonderful revelation the truth can really stand on its own.\r\nLuke 22:35\r\n(Yea, a sword shall pierce through thy own soul also,) that the thoughts of many hearts may be revealed.\r\n\r\nNow, this verse establishes that Jesus is the Rock of Offence so that whatever is in a man\'s heart will be out in the open. This will determine whose God\'s and whose not.\r\nJesus offends many\r\n\r\nJesus offended his family, his cousin John, his friend\'s sisters, his hometown neighbors  to name a few. And it doesn\'t stop there, He keeps on offending people up to the present. All for the benefit of those people who are being offended. \r\n\r\nJeremiah 17:9-10 says, The heart is deceitful above all things, and desperately wicked: who can know it? I the Lord search the heart, I try the reins, even to give every man according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings.\r\n\r\nOnly through pressure from offence can we really know what\'s in our heart. Jesus just need to press the trigger button in us to reveal it.',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59'),
(41105,	1997,	287,	'To welcome offence in my life without fear through the grace of God and to ask for God\'s wisdom to avoid the bait of satan.',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59'),
(41106,	1997,	288,	'Offence, from at different perspective\r\n\r\nAfter this lesson, calling Jesus the Rock of Offence is not offensive anymore. Knowing the reason behind the offence removes the pain it causes.\r\n\r\nOctober 6, 2017, 3:14 PM: I was prompted by the Holy Ghost to pray for John Bevere and his family in the spirit. I saw John getting in touch with our Apostolic brethren in America in one of their church conferences. In Jesus\' name, let John Bevere and his family have the revelation of the mighty God in Christ.',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59',	'2017-10-06 12:40:59'),
(41107,	261,	196,	'Do not complain and keep your focus on God’s faithfulness. David says “feed on His faithfulness”. God hates complaining. We need to treat it like poison. Lets stop complaining about everything. It is rebellion and a lack of the fear of God. Joseph did not complain at all.\r\nWe are the only ones that can destroy the call of God in our life.\r\nWhen you make the decision that you are going to go with God, the flow of the world is contrary to the flow of the kingdom. And you are going to meet resistance and opposition. How you handle it will determine your future because God’s word and promise will come to pass as long as you are not offended.',	'2017-10-06 10:27:10',	'2017-10-06 10:27:10'),
(41108,	261,	197,	'Stop complaining about anything and stay obedient to the harvest. Joseph went through 12 years of just trusting and being faithful to God even though things went horribly wrong in his life.',	'2017-10-06 10:27:10',	'2017-10-06 10:27:10'),
