(42431,	95,	7326,	'Aheb(Hebrew word) Seeking and doing what other people need\r\nThe More you love, the greater your capacity to love the unlovable \r\n- Dont love people because they deserve it, love them because they need it\r\nLove takes work',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36'),
(42432,	95,	7327,	'No Matter what happened, the primary concern of the other is \'are you okay\'\r\n\r\ntalk to God and Say\' Show me about love\'\r\n- God wants to make us more loving but we have to ask \r\n- God wants to give us the deepest part of who he is',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36'),
(42433,	95,	7328,	'nil',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36',	'2017-10-31 19:17:36'),
(42434,	3892,	5986,	'There is natural fear and there is unnatural fear. Fear does not come from God, and God gives us power over the spirit of fear.\r\nWe are to test the spirits to know if they are of God or not. A seducing spirit takes people away from the truth.\r\nHealing is a process. It operates in 3 basic areas, physical, mental, and spiritual.',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35'),
(42435,	3892,	5987,	'To be more aware that we do that wrestle with flesh and bone, but that there are many different spirits trying to distract us, and that God has given us power and victory over them all.',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35'),
(42436,	3892,	5988,	'To better understand that healing is a process and not to get discouraged if it doesn\'t happen right away. Also if God gives us a vision in faith, then to believe him for it, even if we have no idea how its going to happen.',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35',	'2017-10-31 21:15:35'),
(42437,	3892,	6001,	'The miracles of God invites people to come and see.\r\nGod does a miracle when we are obedient and cannot go any further.\r\nThe gifts of God are something that takes faith to operate.',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07'),
(42438,	3892,	6002,	'To become more sensitive to the gifts of the spirit and to have the faith for them to operate.',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07'),
(42439,	3892,	6003,	'The Lord has given us the gifts of the spirit to go forth to reach the world and to empower the Church.',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07',	'2017-10-31 23:45:07'),
(42440,	973,	1336,	'honour is outflow of the fear of the God.\r\nMoses hear God but honour his wife more than God.\r\nWe should be peacemaker not a peacekeeper, we need to confront it for true peace.\r\nBy humility and the fear of the LORD are riches and honor and life.',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27'),
(42441,	973,	1337,	'Praying for wisdom so that I can put God first in making every decisions.',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27'),
(42442,	973,	1338,	'I feel the principles that I am hearing in the classes (TAA and DD) are all talking about one: putting God first and obeying to Him. it has been good study to learn to think if every decisions I make please God. I want to love God more and I don\'t want my love to be just in words but be alive by actions and my life becomes worship for God.',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27',	'2017-11-01 17:56:27'),
(42443,	273,	9156,	'1.	You know someone who is in such a situation\r\n2.	You might be in the situation yourself \r\n3.	You don’t know it yet, but you are about to go into one\r\n“The greater the grief, the fewer the words needed”\r\nIn shock, you need fellowship...in sorrow, you need worship',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42'),
(42444,	273,	9157,	'Take the initiative when ministering to/helping someone in shock or pain, instead of being passive.',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42'),
(42445,	273,	9158,	'Just to have the self-awareness about how shock/pain is a constant factor in the lives of others or myself, so I need to be better equipped to handle such situations, if not for myself, definitely for others.',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42',	'2017-11-01 20:25:42'),
(42446,	4160,	181,	'Offense is the gateway to Satan controlling you\r\nInside the walls the offended have built they sincerely think they are right\r\nThe offended isolate themselves but do so from a desire to do their own will',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40'),
(42447,	4160,	182,	'Not to set my expectations of others based on the role they play in the Kindgom',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40'),
(42448,	4160,	183,	'Offense leads to falling in to the antichrist spirit and agenda without the offended even knowing or realizing it',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40',	'2017-11-02 01:05:40'),
(42449,	259,	9156,	'There are things in our lives that we can\'t go by, we have to go through these 6 phases - Shock, sorrow, struggle, surrender, sanctification, service.\r\nWe don\'t need to have an invitation to share their pain - we need to show up and shut up. The greater the grief, the fewer words needed.\r\nWhen someone is in shock, they need to cry out to God and let other people help them. Never make a major decision - postpone it.',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21'),
(42450,	259,	9157,	'I want to try to help myself to understand their pain. Sometimes I can be too task-oriented that I think about the solution before understanding their pain.',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21'),
(42451,	259,	9158,	'There was a time where a group member  was going to through the shock phase and I actually learned to not speak a lot and just be his friend. It really worked and we had a deeper relationship after that.',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21',	'2017-11-02 04:25:21'),
(42452,	242,	9156,	'Show up & shut up = Ministry of PRESENCE\r\n- When you are in deep deep pain, you don’t need words, you need TOUCH\r\n- The greater the grief, the fewer words needed\r\n- They don’t need words, they need tears – when 1 person is in pain, their whole family is usually in pain too\r\nWhen people are in shock, don’t say:\r\n- Call me if you need anything = forces THEM to take the initiative, do the work\r\n- How can I help? = they DON’T KNOW = they are NUMB\r\n\r\nWhen people are in shock, we should say:\r\n- I would like to do this for you, can I do this for you?\r\n- I would like to bring you dinner on Wed or Thu, which would work best for you?\r\n- IN SHOCK: YOU NEED FELLOWSHIP (not ppl to talk to but ppl to show up in your life)\r\n- Relationships have the potential to demonstrate great fruit people go through pain\r\n- Growing spiritual roots give you fruit gives you vigorousness in the truth',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53'),
(42453,	242,	9157,	'When I go through grief:\r\n- pursue fellowship instead of isolation\r\n\r\nWhen I am helping someone going through grief:\r\n- say less, connect through touch & tears',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53'),
(42454,	242,	9158,	'Did not realise the purpose of the \"Ministry of Presence\" until watching this video.\r\n\r\nThere is a power of presence when words fail.',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53',	'2017-11-02 05:43:53'),
(42455,	88,	9156,	'The greater the grief, the fewer words needed. This is so true.\r\nWhen Rick Warren talked about the ministry of presence: weep with those who weep, they don\'t need words, they need tears.\r\nI really like the point about how to help someone who is in shock: what to say and what not to say. Especially the part about giving the person options to choose from instead of choosing for him.',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29'),
(42456,	88,	9157,	'I am reminded NOT to be quick in offering solutions to people (especially my guys) when they are in shock. I realise that can be my tendency (to preach to them). Instead, I would like to apply the ministry of presence, just to be there for them and let them know that I am there to support them in this time of crisis.',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29'),
(42457,	88,	9158,	'This is so needed especially for us as guys (speaking to myself). It really takes intentional effort on us if we are in grief to slow down, sometimes stop everything and take time to grieve. There is also a need to process the shock. Very often, guys (myself included) self medicate the pain by exercising, working harder, more ministry but we need to be careful because a grief that is not processed can become a hardened place in our heart that blocks off the presence of God.',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29',	'2017-11-02 16:32:29'),
(42458,	279,	9156,	'Shock - Sorrow - Struggle - Surrender - Sanctification - Service.\r\nGod wants to use your experience/struggle to be a service to someone else that is going through it. (Galatians 6:2) Take shock and turn it into service, someone saving grace.\r\nHow to help a friend in Shock:\r\n1) Show Up ( and shut up!) - ministry of presence\r\n2) Share their pain\r\nThe greater the grief, the few words needed.\r\nWe honor GOD when we depend on Him rather than our own abilities.',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06'),
(42459,	279,	9157,	'Be readily, to share my struggles(testimony) when God calls upon it.',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06'),
(42460,	279,	9158,	'Got to have roots to have fruits',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06',	'2017-11-02 18:05:06'),
(42461,	4149,	5686,	'We have to have a genuine passion to reach the lost souls in our worlds. If we don’t have a desperation to to see people’s lives changed, we have lost the point.\r\nGod will not bring you to the point of birth and not bring it to pass. He will give you the things He has promised.\r\nWe have got to get to a place of desperation that we would rather die than not see lives saved and changed forever!',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30'),
(42462,	4149,	5687,	'I desire to develop an attitude of prayer and perseverance in my everyday life!',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30'),
(42463,	4149,	5688,	'I am excited to hear a different perspective on prayer then what has been taught many different ways. I look forward to growing my knowledge of the power of prayer more.',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30',	'2017-11-07 17:47:30'),
(42464,	279,	9171,	'Change is inevitable; it\'s unhealthy to deny loss. You don\'t grow in parties; you grow in the valleys.\r\nJesus is the perfect man as the example for us also grief; how about us? You don\'t get over Grief, you get THROUGH it!\r\nIf I don\'t let it out in healthy ways, I\'m going to act it out in unhealthy ways.',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02'),
(42465,	279,	9172,	'FEAR NOT! in any situation of our lives. Remember Shadow don\'t kill/injure you; always know when there is a shadow, means your back is against the light thus it\'s time to repent and fix your eyes upon the finish work at Calvary, so He will direct your path',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02'),
(42466,	279,	9173,	'Grief is how you deal with your losses and move on.',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02',	'2017-11-02 18:54:02'),
(42467,	28,	9156,	'How do you help a friend in shock?\r\n\r\n1. Show up\r\n-	You don’t have to say anything\r\n-	Just show up and shut up\r\n\r\n2. Share their pain\r\n-	The ministry of presence\r\n-	Weep with those who weep\r\n-	They don’t need words, they need tears\r\n\r\n3. Take the initiative\r\n-	Do good – any practical thing you can do\r\n-	Don’t say – “Call me if you need anything” >> You are forcing them to take the initiative\r\n-	Don’t ask – “How can I help?” >> They are in shock and don’t know what help they need\r\n-	You are forcing them to think and they can’t think\r\n-	You want to give them options – E.g. I would like to bring you dinner, would Wednesday or Thursday work best?\r\nWhat do you do when you are in a catastrophe?\r\n\r\n1.	Cry out to God\r\n-	Psalm 50:15 (NASB)\r\no	You honour God when you call out to Him for help because you are depending on Him\r\n-	Lamentations 2:19 (NCV)\r\no	When you are in shock, you can’t sleep\r\no	What do you do when you can’t sleep, cry out to God\r\no	Open up your heart to God\r\n\r\n2.	Let others help\r\n-	Never try to make a major decision when you are in shock\r\n-	Don’t act like it didn’t happen, it did\r\n-	Probers 17:17\r\no	When you are in shock, notice who shows up and who doesn’t (but don’t judge those who don’t show up because they may be dealing with their own pain)\r\no	Real friends walk in when everyone else walks out\r\no	Let other people help you \r\no	Natural reaction is to withdraw\r\no	In shock, you need fellowship, you need people to show up in your life\r\nThere is a way to prepare yourself for an emotional disaster – you can prepare an emotional catastrophe now. We can be shock-resistant.\r\n\r\n1.	Cultivate stronger relationships\r\n-	God never intended you to go through life alone\r\n-	Your spiritual family is going to last longer than you physical family\r\n-	The best time for you to build a safety net is before a crisis happens\r\n\r\n2.	Grow spiritual roots\r\n-	So that when the heat is on, you don’t tumble away\r\n-	It’s what you know that gets you through\r\n-	You got to have roots to have the fruits',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04'),
(42468,	28,	9157,	'I think one point I will endeavour to apply is to take the initiaitve to help when someone I know is in pain.',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04'),
(42469,	28,	9158,	'I think what I really got from this video is “the ministry of presence”. Showing up, sharing their pain and taking the initiative to help is really the best thing you can do for someone who is deep pain. It’s not so much about what you say. It’s just about you being there for them.\r\n\r\nI found the part about taking initiative to help by offering choices extremely useful. It is so true that a person in shock doesn’t know what help they need at that time. We also do not want to put it on them to ask us for help. We have to be proactive in offering help in a way they can best receive during this stage of shock.',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04',	'2017-11-02 18:50:04'),
(42470,	88,	9171,	'Grief is healthy. \r\na.	It is the only healthy response to a loss. It is unhealthy to deny a loss. \r\nb.	Grief is helpful. Grief is God’s tool for getting you through the transitions of life. \r\nc.	Jesus experienced grief as well. \r\nd.	Sadness is not weakness. Weak men are afraid of showing their emotions.\r\nIf I don’t let it out in healthy ways, I am going to act it out in unhealthy ways. This is so true.\r\nGod gives us the opportunity to lament to him. We can complain to him about our struggles. A lament is a passionate expression of grief to God. An act of worship that includes arguing or complaining to God. Cry out to God.',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55'),
(42471,	88,	9172,	'I realize that there are things in my life there I have not taken the time to grieve over. For example: me not being able to sign on in the Armed Forces. I believe that God has given me the grace to obey Him in this area but it is sometimes really difficult not to think about the possibility and feel sad about it. I know that I will need to continue to trust God and list down the different areas of my life which I need to grieve over.',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55'),
(42472,	88,	9173,	'Nil',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55',	'2017-11-08 19:58:55'),
(42473,	4160,	196,	'No man, woman, child, devil can get you out of the will of God\r\nJoseph\'s brothers said come let\'s kill him and see what may come of his dreams...\r\nGod hates complaining, it is rebellion and the lack of the fear of God',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20'),
(42474,	4160,	197,	'To treat complaining as poison whether it\'s from me or others.',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20'),
(42475,	4160,	198,	'Through everything that we have been through over the past 7 years with losing everything, losing connection with certain members of our family, being reduced to nothing with nothing to fall back on and nothing to rely on but God; we have had every right to complain and to speak out against people who have hurt us, but we knew deep down that there was a purpose to it all. God\'s faithfulness was constantly present and we knew there was a reason for the loss. We have failed some of the lessons God put us through but through this refining process we are ready for anything now.  God has removed people from our lives, even close family, but he has replaced them with like-minded people who are going through the same refining as us and we are an encouragement to each other.',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20',	'2017-11-02 22:51:20'),
(42476,	4129,	181,	'many will be offended. More than 50%\r\nOffense is a snare. Most people don\'t know they are trapped or offended.\r\nWe build up wall to protect ourselves. these stronghold have a progression. Offense, betrayal, hatred and then deception.',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51'),
(42477,	4129,	182,	'All of it.',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51'),
(42478,	4129,	183,	'If offense can be a stronghold for evil then there is a place of revelation and truth that is even stronger for God.',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51',	'2017-11-03 03:08:51'),
(42479,	3849,	5686,	'The comparison between intercessory prayer and authoritative prayer.\r\nConsistently pray and seek to break through to the spiritual realm. To break into authoritative prayer.\r\nIn order to win the lost or impact the world. We have to have a genuine burden for them.',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47'),
(42480,	3849,	5687,	'To pray, pray, pray until God sends the answer. DO NOT GIVE UP or QUIT PRAYING.',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47'),
(42481,	3849,	5688,	'We hear a lot of times that we need to reach the world or different nations. But like he said, it has to be something other then just a nod of the head. We have to have a \"Fire Desire\" to reach the Nations.',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47',	'2017-11-03 05:33:47'),
(42482,	4160,	211,	'Let the Lord judge between us\r\nAm I a man who takes matters into my own hands or do I trust God to judge?\r\nTwo kinds of people: those who love and protect their ministry and those who love God',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16'),
(42483,	4160,	212,	'To continue to allow God to refine me so it will be God that I love and follow and not a position, ministry or title. People can replace me and take my position but no one can take away God from me or the dreams he\'s given me',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16'),
(42484,	4160,	213,	'Wilderness experiences, loss and pain, rejection, offensive unfair treatment is the door to greatness in God and to the fulfillment of His character in us and the dreams he\'s placed in us.',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16',	'2017-11-03 05:52:16'),
(42485,	233,	7341,	'Connection is a heart to heart connection between 2 person. It is more than knowing about someone else.\r\nGod did not make you disconnected or detached. We are either internally driven or externally driven.\r\nUnless a person loves an jndividual just as they are, there will never be transformed. They will just see themselves as a project.',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41'),
(42486,	233,	7342,	'In my small group, I aim to suspend my point of view and allow my friend to express their feelings even if it is not reality.',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41'),
(42487,	233,	7343,	'Na',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41',	'2017-11-04 11:44:41'),
(42488,	4129,	196,	'Joseph obeyed even when things got worse\r\nJoseph could have been offended but instead he feared God and kept serving.\r\nFeed on the faithfulness of God.',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00'),
(42489,	4129,	197,	'I will apply everything but especially the part about feeding on God\'s faithfulness.',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00'),
(42490,	4129,	198,	'The timing of God is never our timing but God is always faithful and keeps HIs word.',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00',	'2017-11-03 07:30:00'),
(42491,	4129,	211,	'God set you under a harsh leader as times\r\nHow you respond to the unfair treatment determines whether you are bitter or better.\r\nGreat growth happens when we trust God in difficult times.',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24'),
(42492,	4129,	212,	'I will be a better leader',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24'),
(42493,	4129,	213,	'I have experienced harsh leaders before. God did use them to refine me.',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24',	'2017-11-04 05:12:24'),
(42494,	4129,	226,	'the idea of roots going down deeper with adversity\r\nOffended people find ways to reason out of their responsibility to change. Cain just complained. He didn\'t consider repentance as an option.\r\nGod chooses where He wants you. If you submit, you will bear much fruit.',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29'),
(42495,	4129,	227,	'everything in the lesson',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29'),
(42496,	4129,	228,	'A lot of people run from confrontations. They pretend but there is an offense hiding under the surface. Roots are shallow because of this. i see this as a major issue in this generation.',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29',	'2017-11-04 06:29:29'),
(42497,	4129,	241,	'There is a blessing when let God defend us.\r\nWhen you rejoice instead of reacting nobody can hurt you.\r\nMature sons need time to develop. offense slows down that process.',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56'),
(42498,	4129,	242,	'Not to defend myself.',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56'),
(42499,	4129,	243,	'Maturity rejoices. immaturity react.',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56',	'2017-11-04 07:03:56'),
(42500,	233,	7356,	'Telling the truth is not the fun part of love, but it is a valuable part. A healthy relationship needs to have a certain level of honesty.\r\nRevenge is bad motives for speaking truth.\r\nThe2 motives for telling the truth is a problem needs to be solved and you want a loving connection.',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30'),
(42501,	233,	7357,	'When confronting my loved one with truth, i endeavor to check my motive.',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30'),
(42502,	233,	7358,	'Na',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30',	'2017-11-09 04:27:30'),
(42503,	3828,	5896,	'Making a mistake doesn\'t mean we lose our authority, however if we don\'t feel like we are in charge we won\'t be able to pray with authority. If we feel uncomfortable while praying it may mean we have some sin in our life or some issue we need to settle, but if our heart condemn us not we will have confidence to pray authoritative prayers.\r\nTo use authoritative prayer, we must be subject to God\'s authority. Our lifestyle must be in line with God\'s commandments. We need to be in right relationship with God so that we can feel the presence of His Spirit living inside us. The peace of God abiding in us is all the confidence we need to know He hears us and anything we pray according to His will, it shall be done.\r\nGeneral prayers get general answers and specific prayers get specific answers. However, we must pray with confidence and when the Spirit is upon us we know that God is speaking now and things are going to happen. Faith means having the confidence that what I\'m praying is being heard of by the Lord and He will act on it because I am praying according to His will.',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41'),
(42504,	3828,	5897,	'Pray daily that I may increase in faith, confidence, and authority. That I will live according to His commands, so He will live in me.',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41'),
(42505,	3828,	5898,	'If I am unsure about my position when praying I need to ask God to forgive me so that I might pray with complete confidence.',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41',	'2017-11-07 05:38:41'),
(42506,	4161,	181,	'1. I love the way that he explained the different levels of expectation.  It was eye opening to see the reason WHY we are more easily offended by the people closest to us.  the bottom line is that people are...people! I can\'t put the same expectations on a human being that I would put on God.  If I put people on a pedestal and expect them to meet my needs, then I am putting them in the place of God in my life...setting them up for failure and setting myself up to become offended.  Instead of walking around holding others to MY expectations; I must seek God and ask what HE requires of me.  Love Him with everything; love my neighbor as my self.\r\n2. An offended person Builds walls.  This is so important because it takes the spotlight off of the \"offender\" and puts it back on the one who has been offended.  Since \"it is impossible that no offenses should come,\" the ball is in MY court!  I must decide what I will do when the enemy lays a snare of offense.  What type of builder will I be?...will I build a fortress of offence, or will I build a bridge and help pave the way to reconciliation?  It\'s actually quite liberation to know that I don\'t HAVE to be offended!  I can walk in love, joy, peace, patience...yes, I can have a \"fruit of the spirit\" salad everyday! :)\r\n3. Once there is offense; false prophets and deception come.  This shows us that offense is blinding! When my eyes are on myself, my rights and my own \"preservation,\" I am blind to the things of God.  Instead of \"looking unto Jesus,\" I can fall into the trap of looking at my problem, looking to myself or seeking tainted counsel from someone else who is offended.  This point reminds me to be \"sober and vigilant\" because there is an enemy out there!...but it\'s not my brother or sister.',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58'),
(42507,	4161,	182,	'I am hoping to apply ALL of them, but this one stands out: unconditional love gives people the \"right\" to hurt us.  instead of giving into the world system that demands God and everyone to acquiesce to my rights, I want to be kingdom minded.  No one has been more rejected, cursed, betrayed or attacked than Jesus...and no one has EVER loved others as much as Him either.  If I really want to be like Him (and I do!) then I must love like He loves.  This life is not about what I can get.  it\'s about what can I give; how can I serve; and how can I love others best.',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58'),
(42508,	4161,	183,	'Great lesson! Looking forward to lesson #2!',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58',	'2017-11-04 18:03:58'),
(42509,	4162,	181,	'The meaning of offense (a bait stick) really stood out.\r\nProverbs 18:19: When we\'re offended, we build bigger walls (strongholds) than a strong city of ancient times!\r\nOur expectations are higher for people we love. So true.',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24'),
(42510,	4162,	182,	'The words of Jesus: \"Freely you have received, freely give . . .\" \r\nThe analogy that John Bevere gives about the contrast between the Dead Sea and the Sea of Galilee was so powerful. I want to give freely.',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24'),
(42511,	4162,	183,	'I love this.  Very biblical and Spirit-led.',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24',	'2017-11-05 06:12:24'),
(42512,	4160,	226,	'Disobedience is the open welcome for offense and once offense is in then it\'s a downhill path to greater sin\r\nMy response to correction and judgement will determine whether I\'m a vagabond wanderer or a tree planted by the water\r\nI don\'t choose where I go or what I do, God chooses for me as he pleases. If I am truly dead to myself and fully submitted to God and the leadership I serve under then I will not be susceptible to offense because i will be aware that it is God in all and through all.',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28'),
(42513,	4160,	227,	'To not only stay planted through submission and obedience but to also not be the reason that weaker or less-rooted trees are offended and thus uproot themselves. Let me not be the door that offense enters in.',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28'),
(42514,	4160,	228,	'There was a time when I felt I had to speak my mind and if I didn\'t speak up for myself then no one would and it got me into more trouble and created more drama and hurt in the process. During the cocoon-like process of God\'s isolation for us I\'ve learned that it is He who has the final say and it is His reasons for everything even if I don\'t understand or get it. So now, when something comes up or something is said, I stay quiet and process it, even if I disagree strongly I will still stay quiet and meditate and pray about it. So when I do finally speak up, if I do, it\'s with care and respect and an understanding that God is doing things for his purpose. I do have my opinion and perspective but seldom share it and will almost never share it immediately unless I feel God\'s approval in that moment. When I\'m asked what I think regarding anything it is difficult for me to give a response because I am hesitant to speak on my own. God has dealt very heavily with me over the years and it is His court that I am always in and speaking the right thing at the right time is a matter of grave concern for me. I fail frequently but I\'m getting better at being seated with Christ in heavenly places.',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28',	'2017-11-06 17:50:28'),
(42515,	4160,	241,	'Through suffering obedience is learned, \"he who has suffered in the flesh has ceased from sin\"\r\nThe blessings that come from obedience and following Christ\'s example are beyond what we\'re able to comprehend.\r\nOffensive behaviors that come at us are opportunities for blessing and growth.',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29'),
(42516,	4160,	242,	'To remember that every attack, every opportunity to be offended and defend myself is the opportunity to be hidden in the cross and allow God to be revealed in me',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29'),
(42517,	4160,	243,	'I see offensive behaviors that come at us as shortcuts to the next level. They\'re early graduation programs to advance to the next level of spiritual maturity and authority.',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29',	'2017-11-06 19:15:29'),
(42518,	4129,	256,	'Revelation knowledge is the key to understanding the Word.\r\nJesus didn\'t water it down. He would rather have disciples with revelation knowledge or no  disciples at all.\r\nPeter could no be offended because he was on the right foundation.',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50'),
(42519,	4129,	257,	'I will seek after the  revelation more and listen always to God.',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50'),
(42520,	4129,	258,	'I learned this lesson along time ago but never tied to offenses. powerful!',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50',	'2017-11-06 22:53:50'),
(42521,	3782,	5881,	'Were going to be at war all the time\r\nWere the ones that set the prisoners free\r\nUntill everybody in this world is saved we have the right and authority, to control the spirit world',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30'),
(42522,	3782,	5882,	'Exercise the authority given to me',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30'),
(42523,	3782,	5883,	'\"We become his voice\"',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30',	'2017-11-07 04:58:30'),
(42524,	4129,	271,	'God uses shaking to remove things we don\'t need in our lives.\r\nSatan put the emphasis on the one things Eve couldn\'t do to change the concept of God in her mind.\r\nPeter had a foundation of revelation that him back to His relationship with Jesus',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51'),
(42525,	4129,	272,	'All',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51'),
(42526,	4129,	273,	'There is a whole lot of shaking going on',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51',	'2017-11-07 07:03:51'),
(42527,	275,	9156,	'How to help a friend in shock\r\n- Show up (ministry of presence)\r\n- Share their pain\r\n- Take the initiative (offer practical thing)\r\nThe greater the grief, the fewer words needed.\r\n\r\nTwo things to do in grief: (1) Cry out to God (Palm 50:15, Lamentations 2:19). When you are in shock, you don\'t sleep. (2) Let others help you. \r\n\r\nNever make a major decision in shock. The natural reaction to pain is withdraw.\r\nDon\'t say, \"Call me if you need anything\". Don\'t put it on them. Don\'t even say, \"How can I help?\". Don\'t put the work on them or force them to think. Say instead, \"lemme give you options...\"\r\n\r\nHow to improve resistance to shock\r\n- cultivate stronger relationships\r\n- grow spiritual roots',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15'),
(42528,	275,	9157,	'I use to think that if I offer help without asking as imposing to the person. But I realize I can still offer them a choice and yet take initiative to help them by asking the question mention by Pastor Warren, \"I would like to do ________, which would be better... _______ (solution A) or ________(solution B)\"\r\n\r\nAs such, I have texted Javier and told him I am going to pass him sampled Soy Milk and asked if Wed or Thursday was better. Going to take more initiative to people in crisis now rather than ask them to let me know.',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15'),
(42529,	275,	9158,	'I like the part when he said that we need fellowship in the midst of crisis because it is true for myself that when I am in crisis, I prefer to hide away and isolate. Also, I use to be very fearful of approaching a hurting person because I do not want to say the wrong thing. Quite excited for the rest of the series to learn how to do so. God has been speaking to me about vulnerability and how I need to open up to let people see the \"real\" me more and how it can be use to lead someone to God.',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15',	'2017-11-07 07:07:15'),
(42530,	4160,	256,	'The church is built on the Rock which is the revealed Word of God\r\nThe constant revealed knowledge from God brings stability which also keeps me from being offended.\r\nAlthough Peter was brash, loud and made alot of mistakes, some serious, he stayed with Jesus because of what had been revealed to him.',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37'),
(42531,	4160,	257,	'Even if I make mistakes and royally screw it all up from the floor up I know what has been revealed to me thus far and that gives me assurance, acceptance and approval and I know that I am his. There is no where else to go.',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37'),
(42532,	4160,	258,	'Hearing the voice of God in my mind communicating with me and actually speaking with me in conversation is the most amazing thing I\'ve ever experienced and it\'s everyday and alot of times it\'s just personal one on one conversation.',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37',	'2017-11-07 07:07:37'),
(42533,	4129,	286,	'Faith in its original form meant to obey\r\nJesus didn\'t change His message to be more acceptable\r\nJesus offended a lot of people',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39'),
(42534,	4129,	287,	'Say the truth with fear',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39'),
(42535,	4129,	288,	'God defends those who don\'t compromise.',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39',	'2017-11-07 07:45:39'),
(42536,	260,	9156,	'The stages of shock, sorrow, struggle, surrender, sanctification and service\r\nIf we are not in a crisis it means we headed into one.\r\nShow up and shut up - its the ministry of presence',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45'),
(42537,	260,	9157,	'To help someone with their pain by showing up because the natural reaction for someone in pain is to withdraw.\r\n\r\nPersonally, for myself is to cultivate stronger relationships.',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45'),
(42538,	260,	9158,	'Past - I can relate to the shock that he is referring to and the emotional blankness and nto being able to process anything\r\nPresent - I will set aside time to cry out to God during DCD, to find Him and soak up in His presence. \r\nFuture - I will need to cultivate relationship and grow spiritual roots',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45',	'2017-11-07 13:31:45'),
(42539,	4149,	5701,	'Before we can be successful at anything for God, we have to develop a consistent prayer life.\r\nWe need to pray until something happens. We have to pray with perseverance.\r\nIt is through prayer that our spiritual man is renewed and strengthened. When you pray, you are breathing in supernatural oxygen to your spirit.',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47'),
(42540,	4149,	5702,	'I am going to strive to make the lifestyle of prayer a habit in my life. I am going to make it a point to pray consistently every day.',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47'),
(42541,	4149,	5703,	'The more we pray the more prayer becomes a part of our very being. Prayer is not just a thing to do, but it becomes a part of who we are.',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47',	'2017-11-07 18:41:47'),
(42542,	4149,	5716,	'The way that we can overcome the enemy is through prayer. Prayer is the tool we can use to defeat the trials in our lives.\r\nBy developing your prayer life, you learn how to connect to the spirit. The more you prayer, the easier it becomes to connect to God’s presence.\r\nGod looks for desperation! When He sees a desperate heart, He is quick to answer the need.',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57'),
(42543,	4149,	5717,	'I am challenging myself to push past the distractions and press into the presence of God. I do not want to get right to my answer or my breakthrough and miss out because I didn’t press far enough.',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57'),
(42544,	4149,	5718,	'God responds to His people when they become desperate. God is near to the broken-hearted and hears the cries of His children. If we will make it a habit to consistently pray ,with desperation, to hear God’s voice, He will provide!',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57',	'2017-11-07 20:07:57'),
(42545,	4149,	5731,	'We have to live in a way that brings glory and honor to God. We are the living apostles of Jesus Christ.\r\nThe church has to live a separated life.\r\nIt is so important that we recognize the voice of God, so when He speaks we are quick to listen.',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50'),
(42546,	4149,	5732,	'As soon as I feel the nudge from the Lord to pray or intercede, I want to act quickly and be sensitive to know that it is truly His voice.',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50'),
(42547,	4149,	5733,	'We represent God with everything we do. Wether it is big or small, we have to represent Christ to the best of our ability.',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50',	'2017-11-07 22:23:50'),
(42548,	4149,	5746,	'The church is the hands, feet, and heart of Jesus. It is the church’s responsibility to go out into the world and destroy the works of the enemy.\r\nGod desires for His will in heaven to be done on earth, but He won’t do it alone. God waits until He hears the prayers from men on earth to act.\r\nUnless we operate in the power God has placed within us, God will not move. We have to unlock the gifts inside of us to allow God to work.',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35'),
(42549,	4149,	5747,	'I want to fully grasp and understand the authority God has placed inside of me in order to be most effective when I pray. I don’t want my lack of knowledge to hinder God’s plan from being fulfilled.',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35'),
(42550,	4149,	5748,	'Sometimes we have to give up our plans, ideas, and will in order to give God room to accomplish what He desires. If we want to see His will done on earth we have to let God’s will be done in our lives.',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35',	'2017-11-08 17:44:35'),
(42551,	3782,	5896,	'We pray with more confidence when we believe what we are praying is Gods will\r\nThe closer you get to the Lord the more you know what he would say or what he wants\r\nGeneral prayers get general answers specific prayers get specific answers',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08'),
(42552,	3782,	5897,	'Get closer to God',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08'),
(42553,	3782,	5898,	'God speaks to us constantly, we just need to open our ears, and obey what he tells us.',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08',	'2017-11-08 04:41:08'),
(42554,	4129,	301,	'Truth is offensive. Jesus offended people all around because the truth cannot change\r\nWe must know when to offending someone is appropriate and when it is not. We must take on the attitude of a servant not a slave\r\nPersonal rights vs preaching truth.',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31'),
(42555,	4129,	302,	'Everything',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31'),
(42556,	4129,	303,	'I completely relate to the giving up of personal rights. There are a lot of people that don’t get this message but it is essential for ministry',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31',	'2017-11-08 05:28:31'),
(42557,	4163,	181,	'Offense come from unmet expectations\r\nFalse prophets are not just in the pulpit\r\nOffense causes agape love to wax cold',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27'),
(42558,	4163,	182,	'I will be mindful of the bait of offense when talking to my church family.',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27'),
(42559,	4163,	183,	'Wonderful first lesson',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27',	'2017-11-08 19:38:27'),
(42560,	242,	9171,	'1.	Grief is God’s tool for getting through the transitions in life\r\na.	Unmourned / unresolved grief is the cause of most of our problems \r\nb.	Grief is absolutely essential to our life, it is healthy, the only healthy response to loss because it is unhealthy to deny a loss\r\nc.	If we don’t grieve our losses, we get stuck\r\nd.	Anxiety, phobias, fears & low self-esteem come from unresolved grief  \r\ne.	Jesus never did anything wrong, never sinned, and yet the Bible says that He grieved\r\n2.	2 unhealthy reactions toward grief: repression & suppression \r\na.	repression = UNCONSCIOUSLY trying to block out painful thoughts\r\nb.	suppression = CONSCIOUSLY trying to block out painful thoughts\r\n3.	Grief is healed in community \r\na.	If I don’t let it out in healthy ways, I’m going to act it out in unhealthy ways\r\nb.	When I swallow my grief, my body rejects it\r\nc.	God grieves with me – my ability to grieve comes from God',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01'),
(42561,	242,	9172,	'Pastor Warren mentioned:\r\n- There is no life without change; there is no change without loss & there is no loss without pain – you lose some of the old to receive some of the new \r\n- All living things change, if you are alive, you will go through changes in life \r\n\r\nThis reminded me of the Chaos Theory that Nancy Laguna mentioned to Judit & myself one day where Judit was reflecting on all the changing she was seeing necessary to happen in her life.\r\n\r\nSis Nancy briefly shared how change & growth was the essence of being alive. \r\n\r\nThis lesson further proves how miserable I will be if I don\'t let the Holy Spirit & the grace of God lead me through grieving through the losses & transitions of life.',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01'),
(42562,	242,	9173,	'“While grief is the most painful emotion we got through in life, it is also the most helpful emotion in life.” – Rick Warren \r\nI am beginning to accept that the pain of grief is actually an asset, a blessing in the “in between” space of different life stages.\r\nNo one teaches you that.\r\nWe are raised to not cry when we are scolded as children. That causes us to eventually shut down emotionally, and that is not healthy or Biblical.\r\nBut God’s grace & love are sufficient to sustain us in facing our fears, bringing healing & restoration into our lives. It is a process.',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01',	'2017-11-30 13:55:01'),
(42563,	3857,	226,	'It is not our responsibility to judge father\'s. It is a father\'s responsibility to judge children.\r\nBeloved, do not avenge yourself. That is God\'s job.\r\nOffended people will gravitate towards one another.',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08'),
(42564,	3857,	227,	'To wait. I can\'t seek vengeance on those that I am apposed to. I have to leave that to God. I also can\'t expect someone to bend to where I\'m currently at on my walk with God. That would be too easy. I have to allow the process to work itself out. When it\'s time to move, I need to be ready.',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08'),
(42565,	3857,	228,	'Adversity causes a trees roots to dig deeper. Since I was on this app last, I believe I was just gaining the nerve to talk to my father after what amounted to 19 of ostracisation. Since then I have Bridget the gap and forgiven him. I even, now bring him to church with me on Sundays and spend a little time afterwards. I even enjoy it a bit. I\'m still hurt and find some things offensive, but that\'s as far as I let them go. Now, months later, I find myself offended by my mother and sister. Who, have not necessarily done anything to me other than find fault in the way that I\'m now looking my life. Because I choose to not expose my children to certain things, that they happen to do freely, they are blaming me for keeping my children from them. Which may kind of be true. But I\'ve also told them why. And I\'m the bad guy for protecting my children from what I was exposed to as a child. So I\'m diving back in to complete my original commitment from a slightly different lense to make sure that I\'m properly grounded here.',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08',	'2018-09-10 05:57:08'),
(42566,	229,	9156,	'The most influential events in your life often catch us unaware. We can\'t go by them, we go through. In fact, we lose things everyday in our lives. So we must learn how to go through it. \r\n- SIX STAGES OF GRIEF:\r\n    - Shock\r\n    - Sorrow\r\n    - Struggle\r\n    - Surrender\r\n    - Sancitification\r\n    - Service\r\nHow do you help a friend in shock?\r\n1. SHOW UP.  \r\nWe don\'t need to say anything. Just show up and shut up. This is the ministry of presence. \r\n- For eg, Job 2:11 - When they heard about Job who went through a crisis, they set out and went to him. They didn\'t wait. When you are in deep, deep pain, you don\'t need words, you need touch. \r\n2, SHARE THEIR PAIN. \r\n- Job 2:12-13 - Before they saw him, they began to weep aloud and tore their robes and throw dust on their heads. In other words, they are saying, they are right there with him. They sat there for 7 days without saying a word, because they saw how great his grief was. \r\n- The greater the grief, the fewer words needed.\r\n- The bible says to weep with those who weep.\r\n- They don\'t need words; they need tears.\r\n3. TAKE THE INITIATIVE\r\n- Prov 3:27 - Whenever you possibly can, do good to those who need it.\r\n- Do good = run an errand, babysit, do laundry, buy food\r\n- What not to do: \"Call me if you need anything\" or \"How can I help?\"\r\n- When someone is in shock, they are numb. Everything is moving in slow motion. So don\'t put the initiative on them - they can\'t think.\r\n- Give them options instead. For eg, \"I\'d like to bring you dinner. Would Wednesday or Thursday be better?\"\r\nAs much as you can prepare yourself for a physical catastrophe, you can prepare yourself for an emotional catastrophe. We can become shock-resistant and handle shocks better.\r\n- HOW TO IMPROVE YOUR RESISTANCE TO SHOCK?\r\n1. CULTIVATE STRONGER RELATIONSHIPS\r\nGod never intended for you to go through life by yourself without any support group. Your spiritual family is going to outlast your earthly family. People grow up, move off and die. But the family of God will last forever. So you need to cultivate strong relationships. The best time to cultivate stronger relationships is NOW, before any bad things happen. \r\n- Ecc 4:9-12 - Two can accomplish more than twice as much as one\r\n\r\n2. GROW SPIRITUAL ROOTS\r\n- When the heat is on, you won\'t dry up and roll away. When tough times come, you need to know God will lead you through.\r\n- Jer 17:7-8 - You got to have the roots, so that you will have the fruits.\r\n- Col 2:6-7 - Trust him for each day\'s problems.',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14'),
(42567,	229,	9157,	'1. When someone is in a crisis, I don\'t need have to say anything. Instead, I just need to show up and take care of their needs. For eg, babysit, buy food, run errands. \r\n2. Build stronger relationships and grow spiritual roots.',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14'),
(42568,	229,	9158,	'1. I thought back to the time when I was grieving for the loss of my loved ones, and recognized the importance of having strong relationships in the Body of Christ is. Because though they can\'t help much, but that support was there. Equally important are the spiritual roots that we cultivate because crisis like these will shake our worlds. \r\n\r\n2. I always thought that people will want to be left alone when they are going through a crisis or a tough time, so I usually just touch and go with a text or two, but this lesson really gave me a paradigm shift in my mindset. I now see that not only do I help by offering comforting words, my presence actually help them much more. I\'ll think of ways to do good to a fellow saint that\'s going through a family crisis in the hyphen group.',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14',	'2017-11-08 16:43:14'),
(42569,	4149,	5761,	'A person has to renew themselves in the Lord daily. You can not keep pouring out and engaging in spiritual warfare if you don’t have anything to give.\r\nWhen you are consistent in prayer and are constantly praying for the will of God, the Lord takes note and is quick to listen.\r\nWe have to pray that God would protect us form the acts of the enemy. If we don’t have God’s protection, we will not be able to withstand the trials of this life.',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22'),
(42570,	4149,	5762,	'I need God’s blood to completely cover my life daily. If I am not saturated in His blood the enemy will have ground to resist',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22'),
(42571,	4149,	5763,	'I am going to adapt these self request payers into my prayer time to make sure that I remain completely immersed in the blood of Jesus.',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22',	'2017-11-08 18:22:22'),
(42572,	28,	9171,	'Loss is unavoidable but grief is a choice\r\n-	A lot of people choose not to grieve; they stuff it, they deny it – that’s a big mistake\r\n-	There is no life without change, there is no change without loss, there is no loss without pain\r\n-	Grieve is a choice\r\n-	You have to choose to let grieve in and allow yourself to feel it\r\n-	We have thousand of losses in life (e.g. health, job, friends)\r\n-	Because grieve is unpleasant, most people just avoid it and that is the cause of many problems (unresolved grieve)\r\n\r\nGrieve is healthy\r\n-	It is the only healthy response when you have a loss\r\n-	It is unhealthy to deny a loss\r\n-	Grieve is the most painful emotion but it is also the most helpful emotion\r\n-	Grieve is God’s tool for getting you through the transitions of life\r\n-	If you don’t grieve in your losses, you get stuck\r\n-	Jesus grieved; He wept when Lazarus died (John 11:33,36 NLT)\r\n-	He was a man acquainted with grief\r\n-	Sadness is not weakness\r\n-	Weak men are afraid of showing their emotions\r\n-	2 unhealthy reactions to grief (loss)\r\no	Repression – Unconsciously try to block out painful thoughts\r\no	Suppression – Consciously trying to block painful thoughts \r\n-	If I don’t let it out in healthy ways, I’m going to act it out in unhealthy ways\r\n-	When I swallow the grieve, my body rejects it\r\n-	God never intended emotions to be bottled up inside of us\r\nGod grieves with me\r\n-	Your whole ability to grieve comes from God\r\n-	You are created in the image of God; the reason you grieve is because God grieves\r\n-	Your ability to grieve is what makes you different from animals\r\n-	When you choose to live in denial, you are denying the very thing that makes you like God in His image\r\n-	God also grieves with us – He is a sympathetic God, He is not aloof\r\n-	God isn’t standing on the sidelines, but He actually enters into your grieve\r\n-	Psalms 34:18 (NIV)\r\n\r\nGrief is healed in community\r\n-	You are not going to get well on your own\r\n-	God hates loneliness (He made us to love Him and love each other)\r\n-	You need relationships, community \r\n-	Galatians 6:2 (NIV)\r\n-	When you are in pain, I’m supposed to carry your pain – we are to support each other\r\n-	Romans 12:5 (TLB) – share their sorrow\r\n-	Revealing your feelings is the beginning of healing\r\n4 Things to Help You get Unstuck\r\n\r\n1.	List the losses I’ve never grieved\r\n-	Go back and take an inventory of your life\r\n-	Where have I had major losses in my life?\r\n-	I can’t get past it until I’ve acknowledged it\r\n-	Jesus said grief is the key to comfort (Matthew 5:4)\r\n-	Cover-ups don’t get comforted\r\n-	Why don’t we allow ourselves to grieve?\r\no	Fear of overwhelming emotions\r\no	Fear of never recovering\r\n-	If you are afraid to grieve, you need to claim Psalm 23:4\r\no	Walk through the valley – you are not going to stay stuck there\r\no	Shadow of death – shadows make things look bigger than they are\r\no	Grief doesn’t paralyse, fear does\r\n\r\n2.	Identify what I’ve really lost\r\n-	What did I really lose in this situation?\r\n-	Did I lose trust? Did I lose my credibility? Did I lose my childhood? Did I lose my innocence?\r\n\r\n3.	Have the courage to lament\r\n-	Lament – A passionate expression of grief to God; an act of worship that can include arguing or complaining to God (not about God)\r\n-	There’s even a book in the Bible about Jeremiah’s lamentations\r\n-	Even the book of Psalms contains laments\r\n-	Talk to God!\r\n\r\n4.	Ask Jesus to heal your broken heart\r\n-	He made us and is close to the broken hearted\r\n-	Psalm 103:13-14\r\n-	Luke 4:18 – Jesus came to heal the broken hearted\r\n-	In your pain, look to Jesus\r\n-	Wherever there is a shadow, there is a light\r\n-	When you walk through the valley of shadow of death, turn your back on the shadow and look at the light',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36'),
(42573,	28,	9172,	'To choose to grieve when I experience a loss.',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36'),
(42574,	28,	9173,	'This was a really good lesson. It’s so true that we can grieve about many different things. I remembered when I first started working, I felt like I was dying on the inside. I came home from my first day at work crying. There was nothing wrong the job or my colleagues. But I felt a loss - loss of freedom, loss of my identity and lifestyle as a student. I didn’t realize it then, but I was grieving.\r\n\r\nI see how important it is to identify what is it that we lost. If not, it will just be a bad feeling that we don’t know how to deal with. The importance of acknowledging that loss instead of ignoring it / numbing it / denying it is crucial to our healing. \r\n\r\nAm thankful for this lesson! Will also try to help others who are grieving identify what is it exactly they have lost. Thank you!',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36',	'2017-11-08 19:05:36'),
(42575,	4187,	3526,	'No one can be saved without a fear of the Lord. I like the example of Lot\'s future son- in -laws, they lacked a fear in the Lord and therefore were able to laugh at Lot\'s warning. If they would have had that fear they would have trusted the warning from God.\r\nThe amount of sin in Nineveh compared to the sins of Sodom and Gomorrah. The sins of Nineveh  were in God\'s face, the people lacked total fear of God (and respect ).\r\nThe fear of the Lord is having the mind of Christ.',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26'),
(42576,	4187,	3527,	'To fear God with a reverence and a respect.',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26'),
(42577,	4187,	3528,	'N/A',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26',	'2017-11-11 03:17:26'),
(42578,	4149,	5776,	'If we have a guilty conscience we can not have to adequate faith to see God perform miracles. We need to get rid of guilt and claim God’s blood over our lives.\r\nDo not go out and challenge temptation to come to you. Instead ask God to lead you ways from that so the you can focus on the things of the Lord.\r\nForgiveness is so important. If we can forgive others, or ourselves, then we have not fully grasped God’s forgiveness. If the creator of the universe can forgive us, then we should be able to forgive others without question.',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34'),
(42579,	4149,	5777,	'I want God to have complete control in my life. I am going to make it a point to always self reflect and make sure that there isn’t anything in my spirit that would hinder the moving of God’s presence. Nothing is worth not reaching my full potential in God.',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34'),
(42580,	4149,	5778,	'We need to make sure that our spirits empty of sin so when God speaks to us we are already tuned into His presence. We need to always be ready to intercede or go into spiritual warfare when God instructs.',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34',	'2017-11-08 19:13:34'),
(42581,	4184,	3526,	'Something that I believe Christians take for granted is the Presence of God.   The thing that resonated with me the most was when he said \"the Privilege of His Presence.\"  It\'s a privilege to be in His Presence and most of the time we come to church or go to prayer just expecting Him to be there - which He is - taking for granted what a privilege it really is.\r\nN/A\r\nN/A',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54'),
(42582,	4184,	3527,	'To remember what a privilege it is to enter into His Presence.',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54'),
(42583,	4184,	3528,	'N/A',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54',	'2017-11-09 22:35:54'),
(42584,	233,	7371,	'You can do a lot to help others move into healing without being trained. We can be a support system for those who are currently in counselling\r\nWhen we help others heal, we are essentially touching on a very fragile part of their heart. As such, we need to be mentored and handle each situation with care.\r\nWe need to be a dependable and safe if we wish to help someone heal. We need to be a confidant that is stable.',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11'),
(42585,	233,	7372,	'I endeavor to help people heal by active listening to their problems before giving advice.',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11'),
(42586,	233,	7373,	'Na',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11',	'2017-11-13 11:38:11'),
(42587,	260,	9171,	'Grieving is necessary and a choice. Unresolved grief brings more issues than the original source of loss and pain. It is unhealthy to deny a loss by no grieving as it helps us with transitions of life.\r\nIf I don\'t let out in healthy ways, I\'m going to act it out in unhealthy ways.\r\nWe cannot rush grief. It has it own timetable. We don\'t get over grief, we get through it.',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05'),
(42588,	260,	9172,	'Not to get over the grief, allow it to take its time. But get through it because grief is a season - a time of mourning.',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05'),
(42589,	260,	9173,	'I like the part where he says if we don\'t let out in healthy ways we will act out in unhealthy ways. It gives me a new perspectives on people who might be acting out because of unresolved grief that they choose not to address.',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05',	'2017-11-09 05:01:05'),
(42590,	88,	9186,	'It is OK to struggle with God. The opposite of struggling with God is that you are running away from Him and avoiding Him. Struggling with God is a face to face encounter.\r\nC: Complain – Usually in the form of a question \r\nA: Appeal – To God’s nature, character, attributes \r\nR: Remind – Remind God of what He said, remind God of His reputation \r\nE: Express – Express trust in God’s wisdom\r\nThe way you win a fight with God is by surrendering. Surrendering all your unanswered questions to God, trust in Him. Surrender control to God.',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50'),
(42591,	88,	9187,	'This principle of lamenting is something that I have never really tried before. I\'ve always been told not to be like the children of Israel and complain about life but I\'m realizing through this teaching that there is a place for complaining in the form of lament but it must be to God, not about God. I believe that when I am honest with God about how I really feel, that means that I\'m authentic with Him. Perhaps, that is one way of worshiping in Spirit and in Truth. So, instead of \"sucking it up and tolerating\" when I go through difficult times or feel that I have been treated unjustly, something that I will apply is to complain to God using the model that was taught in this video.',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50'),
(42592,	88,	9188,	'In the previous lesson, I wrote in the reflection that I didn\'t feel that I had allowed myself to grieve over not being able to sign on to the army and how it still affects me periodically. But today, I managed to talk to God about it and take some time to slow down and grieve about it. I know that it will be a process to trust that God knows best in this matter but I praise God that He gave me an opportunity to open up to Him in this area of my life.',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50',	'2017-11-09 16:00:50'),
(42593,	4129,	316,	'We cannot categorize sin. All sin will take you to hell\r\nThe one who cannot forgive is one who has forgotten what he was forgiven of.\r\nHell is what we deserve, but Jesus freely forgave us. This should motivate us to forgive others',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49'),
(42594,	4129,	317,	'Not to put people in a category.',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49'),
(42595,	4129,	318,	'Forgiveness is my own key to freedom. If I don\'t forgive I stay bound.',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49',	'2017-11-09 22:46:49'),
(42596,	4181,	181,	'The devils trap is to get offended.\r\nProverbs 18:19\n\nBeing isolated will build strong holds.\r\nSheep in wolves clothing',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45'),
(42597,	4181,	182,	'To keep in mind that the trap of the devil is to become offended with any simple thing.',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45'),
(42598,	4181,	183,	'I will not let small things offend me, because I know that it is the trap.',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45',	'2017-11-09 23:09:45'),
(42599,	4184,	3541,	'His presence will not be found if the atmosphere isn’t where He is held with the utmost respect.  The fear of the Lord creates an atmosphere for the Lord to move/work\r\nN/A\r\nN/A',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30'),
(42600,	4184,	3542,	'N/A',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30'),
(42601,	4184,	3543,	'N/A',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30',	'2017-11-16 23:39:30'),
(42602,	4181,	196,	'Gossip\r\nComplaining\r\nThe battles comes right before the harvest.',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34'),
(42603,	4181,	197,	'Knowing that the test comes before something great God makes happen in my life.\nNo complaining!',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34'),
(42604,	4181,	198,	'I find myself complaining especially in times of trial but I need to discern it correctly and know God is Faithful and preparing me for a great Harvest in my life.',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34',	'2017-11-09 23:49:34'),
(42605,	4187,	3541,	'You cannot  come into the presence  of God without  a fear of God.\r\nYou won\'t  find the presence of God in a place where He is not feared.\r\nYou cannot have  a  true fear of the Lord unless you understand  His greatness.',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19'),
(42606,	4187,	3542,	'Get a better understanding of His word and His greatness to gain a greater fear of the Lord.',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19'),
(42607,	4187,	3543,	'Moses  even after all he witnessed all the miracles God had done , he  still desired to see God\'s face. He still wanted more.',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19',	'2017-11-11 03:30:19'),
(42608,	4129,	331,	'Bitterness will defile you. We must examine ourselves.\r\nBitterness is unfulfilled revenge.\r\nHoliness means to think and act like God. it means to rise above.',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36'),
(42609,	4129,	332,	'Everything!',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36'),
(42610,	4129,	333,	'Several things stood out. Mainly, the different kinds of thinking. Revenge vs, holiness.',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36',	'2017-11-10 04:01:36'),
(42611,	259,	9171,	'A lot of people want to go through life without going through grieve. We have to allow grieve in - we choose to grieve or avoid it. When we avoid it, we get stuck at that stage.\r\nGrieve is a healthy response to loss. It\'s the most painful but helpful emotion we can have. If I don\'t let it out in healthy ways, I\'m going to act it out in unhealthy ways.\r\nGrieve is healed in community. Nobody gets healed alone. Galatians 6:2 - we are supposed to carry each other\'s grieve and support each other. We need to take time to grieve because grieve has it\'s own timetable - we don\'t get over grieve, we get through it.',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19'),
(42612,	259,	9172,	'To allow myself to properly grieve when I deal with loss.',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19'),
(42613,	259,	9173,	'I remember that year when I was doing Kids Camp and there were alot of issues and I was under a lot of stress. But I didn\'t grieve properly after the camp was over and repress my painful thoughts. I need to give myself time to grieve and allow people to help me in my grieving process.',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19',	'2017-11-10 05:00:19'),
(42614,	4158,	181,	'the percentage of people that actually accept that they are offended\r\nSkandolon-the bait stick of a trap\r\nHow we have strongholds in our mind- walls that we build ourselves',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33'),
(42615,	4158,	182,	'Expectations that you have and to never let it get as far as hatred',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33'),
(42616,	4158,	183,	'none',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33',	'2017-11-10 05:51:33'),
(42617,	275,	9171,	'There is no change without loss\r\nThere is no loss without pain\r\nGrief does not only happen in funerals. We have thousand of losses in our lives. \r\nPeople try to avoid grief because it is unpleasant. \r\nUnmourned grief creates a lot of problems. You are stuck at that stage.\r\nSadness are not weakness.\r\nWeak men are afraid of being emotional\r\nIf i don\'t let it out in healthy ways, I am going to act it out in unhealthy ways\r\nWhen I swallow my grief, my stomach rejects it\r\nGod hates loneliness\r\n\r\nYou got to acknowledge, accept it an feel it to get through your pain. \r\nPeople that dare not grieve are fearful. What fears?',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11'),
(42618,	275,	9172,	'Allowing myself to slow down and feel and process my emotions and crying it out.',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11'),
(42619,	275,	9173,	'I have been spending more time being open and vulnerable to Brenda and basically the people around me. I am not use to speaking what I think or feel. In my desire to process things first, I end up bottling it up inside.  I am trying to strike a balance between being real, and making sure my words are filtered at the same time. While it is true i feel extreme sadness more recently, I can also feel extreme joy and intimacy with people around me more as well.',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11',	'2017-11-10 06:16:11'),
(42620,	4183,	181,	'Having expectations in people gives opening to be offended\r\nWe Walk In the Flesh but we do not war in the flesh\r\nWhoever hates his brother is a murderer',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59'),
(42621,	4183,	182,	'Give God\'s love freely',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59'),
(42622,	4183,	183,	'Do not isolate myself',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59',	'2017-11-10 06:27:59'),
(42623,	4129,	346,	'it is a spiritual exercise to pray for those who abuse us.\r\nThe goal of a meeting with someone who has offended you is reconciliation . create an atmosphere for reconciliation\r\nWhen we hold an offense, we sin against God.',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56'),
(42624,	4129,	347,	'God\'s ways',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56'),
(42625,	4129,	348,	'Love this lesson!',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56',	'2017-11-10 08:10:56'),
(42626,	281,	9156,	'Ministry of presence - show up and shut up\r\nPeople who are in shock need friends/company.\r\nThe deeper the grief the fewer words needed.',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48'),
(42627,	281,	9157,	'I’ve always been concerned about being too intrusive when people are hurting or going through a  difficult time. I don’t want to seem pushy or too in your face so I offer my help but wait for their response thinking it will give them space. But now that I’ve heard this teaching, I’ll take the intitiaitve boldly and without hesitation knowing that is what they need.',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48'),
(42628,	281,	9158,	'Feel/share people’s pain. Just be there without needing to say anything. Practice the ministry of presence. Show up when ppl are hurting/going through a difficult time.',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48',	'2017-11-10 19:35:48'),
(42629,	4165,	181,	'That \"many\" should be offended actually refers to a percentage of 51% or higher and that it is warned about as a sign of the endtimes.\r\nThe gradual digression of an offense turning to betrayal then to actual hatred.\r\nHis definition of betrayal being \"Protecting myself at the expense of a relationship in my life.\"  This makes me realize there are small betrayals that we make all the time...not just large, obvious betrayals.',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39'),
(42630,	4165,	182,	'Praying to see areas of my life where I may betray others to keep myself protected or my image protected. Asking God to show me if there are areas of unforgiveness still in me from people that have offended me. Praying to be quick to address areas of offense in my life.  Praying for discernment to detect the wolves in sheep clothing and for God\'s wisdom for next steps with them.',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39'),
(42631,	4165,	183,	'Powerful and revelatory material. Definitely shines a flashlight on my  heart and soul.',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39',	'2017-11-10 22:58:39'),
(42632,	4186,	3526,	'I like that he established the importance of a foundation.\r\nHaving the fear of the Lord has an element of awe and respect\r\nIt is possible for a Christian to have some knowledge but lack Wisdom.',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32'),
(42633,	4186,	3527,	'The focus on the foundation',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32'),
(42634,	4186,	3528,	'If we truly feared the Lord, we would approach our daily tasks according to the scripture that says do everything as into the Lord. Col 3',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32',	'2017-11-11 03:26:32'),
(42635,	4186,	3541,	'There is a very distinct difference between God as our father and Fear of the Lord that the presence of God demands\r\nNobody liked Job\r\nThe shear magnitude of God is awesome.',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54'),
(42636,	4186,	3542,	'I will endure to remember to reverence God when bringing petitions to Him.',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54'),
(42637,	4186,	3543,	'No',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54',	'2017-11-27 02:31:54'),
(42638,	4163,	196,	'God’s plan will come to pass as long as I don’t get offended.\r\nSometimes reciting his promises is not enough, and we need to hold on to his faithfulness.\r\nComplaining is telling God that he is incompetent.',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38'),
(42639,	4163,	197,	'Not complaining when things don’t go my way.',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38'),
(42640,	4163,	198,	'When you resolve not to be offended you seem to get met by the opportunity.',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38',	'2017-11-11 05:37:38'),
(42641,	279,	9186,	'3 ways we struggle:\r\nPeople\r\nSelf\r\nGod\r\nWe doubt His wisdom and we want to be in Control.\r\nGod loves it when you struggle with Him, God rather you fighting Him than you fleeing him. Wrestling is a face to face encounter. God wants you to have the revelation by yourself. \r\nC - Complain, A - Appeal, R - Remind & E - Express Trust\r\nWe need to come to a place where we are tired of tolerating. Two keys of complaint: Complaint to God, not ABOUT God, Complain in Faith',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20'),
(42642,	279,	9187,	'Surrendering myself to God always and daily!! The best of winning is to give up control because ultimately to track it back, I\'m really not in control at all',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20'),
(42643,	279,	9188,	'I like the sentence that he mentioned, all of God\'s giant walked with a limp, speaking from a human point of view: we want to reflect that all is well and good, walking with a limp is never a consideration. So it\'s ok to walk with a limp in our lives knowing that God is in charge after all. Quoting what Bishop Ellis always says, I rather please the ONE that matters than to please the multitude.',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20',	'2017-11-16 18:27:20'),
(42644,	4129,	1,	'We meet authority when we meet God. God\'s authority are one and the same.\r\nGod puts one man over a ministry. We answer to God for how faithful we were to that man of God.\r\nRebellion is bondage. Submission is freedom.',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59'),
(42645,	4129,	2,	'I will live under cover.',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59'),
(42646,	4129,	3,	'I have learned this the hard way.',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59',	'2017-11-11 08:20:59'),
(42647,	28,	9186,	'Life is a struggle. There are 3 ways we struggle:\r\n\r\n1.	With other people\r\n•	Our relationships are broken because of sin\r\n•	We experience competition, conflict, misunderstandings, disappointments\r\n•	Jacob struggled with his brother Esau, he struggled with two wives, he struggled with his in-laws, he struggled with his 12 sons\r\n\r\n2.	With ourselves\r\n•	Your biggest battle is inside you\r\n•	Struggle with fears, flaws, temptations, insecurities, guilt, regret, insecurities etc.\r\n•	Romans 7:15-23 (NLT)\r\n\r\n3.	With God\r\n•	Most of your struggles with others and yourself is rooted in your struggle with God\r\n•	2 reasons why we struggle with God\r\no	We doubt His wisdom\r\no	We want to be in control\r\n•	Whenever we doubt God\'s wisdom, we try to be God because we think we know better than God\r\n•	Jacob demonstrates struggling with God\r\n•	Hosea 12:3 (NIV)\r\no	As a baby, Jacob struggled with Esau\r\no	As a man, Jacob struggled with God\r\nJacob\'s wrestle with God\r\no	God could have easily won Jacob in this wrestle\r\no	But He lets this struggle go on\r\no	God loves it when we wrestle and struggle with Him\r\no	Because the opposite of struggling with God, is walking away from Him and avoiding Him\r\no	God would rather you fight with Him than you flee from Him\r\no	Wrestling is a face-to-face encounter; it is the most intimate sport\r\no	God also knew what was Jacob\'s name - God has never missed a day in Jacob\'s life\r\no	But God wanted Jacob to acknowledge who he was\r\no	Many times when God asks us a question, He already knows the answer and wants to reveal the answer to us\r\no	Jacob \"won\" the wrestle (he prevailed)\r\no	Israel means \"struggles with God\" and also \"a prince with God\"\r\no	God does His deepest work in your life in your identity\r\no	Until God changes the way you see yourself, you are going to struggle for the rest of your life\r\nWhat To Do When I am in a Struggle with God? / How to Argue with God and Win?\r\n\r\nC - Complain\r\n•	In the Bible, usually these complains come in the form of questions\r\n•	When I don\'t like what\'s going on in my life, I tell God what is unfair or painful\r\n•	This is the start of a lament\r\n•	Job 13:15-25 (Good News Translation)\r\n•	You can lament out of anger, out of frustration, out of fatigue, out of disappointment, out of fear\r\n•	What are you tired of tolerating in your life?\r\n•	Whatever that is, you need to turn that in a lament\r\n•	Here are the keys to lamenting\r\no	Complain to God not about God (the children of Israel complained about God in the wilderness)\r\no	Complain in faith (I believe You are going to hear me on this)\r\n\r\nA - Appeal\r\n•	Appeal to God\'s nature\r\n•	When you read the Psalms, you see them complaining to God but you see them still making an appeal to God\'s nature, and asking God for help\r\n•	God loves it when you do this\r\n•	I know You are a good God, I know You are a just God, I know You are all powerful\r\n\r\nR - Remind\r\n•	Remind God of what He has said in His Word\r\n•	Remind God of His promises and appeal to His reputation\r\n\r\nE - Express Trust\r\n•	Express my total trust in God\r\n•	When you see David\'s psalms, he ends with choosing to trust in God\r\n•	Lord, I trust Your goodness, wisdom, plans even in the bad things that has happened and I don\'t understand\r\n\r\nThe way you win a fight with God is by surrendering. I surrender all my unanswered questions. And that gives me comfort and power that I don\'t have on my own. The only way you are going to win in the struggle of life is to give up control. The most dangerous disease you are going to have is to think that you are in control, when you are not. The greatest things in your life is out of your control.',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11'),
(42648,	28,	9187,	'To complain, appeal, remind and express my total trust in Him when I face a struggle.',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11'),
(42649,	28,	9188,	'Wow. I don\'t even know where to begin. This was such a powerful lesson. What stood out to me was how God likes us to wrestle with Him - to be real with Him. Because by not doing so, we are putting up a facade, we are avoiding Him. Sometimes, I think we go into the \"Praise the Lord, I know everything is going to be okay\" mode too quickly. And the truth is, our hearts don\'t even believe what we are saying. It\'s liberating to know that God likes it when we struggle with Him. He likes it when we are being real and honest. However, it\'s not also about staying in the complaining phase. We also need to move on to the other stages of appealing, reminding and expressing trust. Complaining is a means to an end - surrender. \r\n\r\nI think this is also especially useful when we counsel people who are experiencing a loss. As Christians, we can be so used to saying the politically correct answer out of habit. But this lesson has helped me realize that I need to help others come to a point of struggling face-to-face with God so that they can eventually surrender their unanswered questions to Him.\r\n\r\nGreat lesson. Thank you so much for this training.',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11',	'2017-11-11 10:53:11'),
(42650,	3782,	5911,	'If you\'re going to pray a prayer of authority you also learn to submit yourself to those who are in authority.\r\nWe submit our flesh to the authority of  God when we fast\r\nIf you\'ll fast I\'ll bring you out of obscurity and your darkest point will be brighter than the noon day',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19'),
(42651,	3782,	5912,	'I will fast more',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19'),
(42652,	3782,	5913,	'I knew that fasting was breaking my flesh but I didn\'t know that it was a form of submission to God.',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19',	'2017-11-11 15:43:19'),
(42653,	4187,	3556,	'Adam and Eve listened to the Serpent\'s lie , believing that they would have the mind of God when eating the fruit, instead in the vanity of Adam\'s mind he reduced God down to his level, thats why they feel into sin.\r\nWe have reduced Jesus down to the image of us, the image  of someone just like us. We have made Him \"our friend\" \"our buddy\", when He is our God. Yes, He can be our friend too but only IF we do whatever He has commanded  us to do.\r\nIf you bring the people into the  promise land without introducing them to Jesus  they will make the promise  land a god.',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07'),
(42654,	4187,	3557,	'Very convicting message. Nothing is hidden from God. We forget that He sees all. We say things and do things that Jesus died for',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07'),
(42655,	4187,	3558,	'N/a',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07',	'2017-11-11 18:44:07'),
(42656,	3782,	5926,	'We are able to control hell with authoritative prayer\r\nIf I don\'t take control of the spirits in advance they are going to be there trying to affect things\r\nI recognize in that particular service something can change eternity for some one whose there',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45'),
(42657,	3782,	5927,	'I will Pray for the service before the service',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45'),
(42658,	3782,	5928,	'I understand now that some people are not able to make it to church because that\'s the way God ordained it ,so that all who need to receive , receive all that they need to receive. It all happens as it should.',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45',	'2017-11-11 16:53:45'),
(42659,	4158,	196,	'Absolutely no one can get you out of the will of GOD\r\nJoseph never once complained and it took almost 12 years for God purpose to start taking place\r\nJoseph never got bitter in his circumstances and never lost heart and still ministered in the dungeon even after being there for years',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15'),
(42660,	4158,	197,	'Make an active choice of life',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15'),
(42661,	4158,	198,	'Joseph used his power to still bless his family after the betrayal  instead of killing or ignoring them',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15',	'2017-11-12 05:39:15'),
(42662,	3784,	5821,	'We determine how the tap flows\r\nOne spirit one mind and one accord.\r\nMove in unity',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52'),
(42663,	3784,	5822,	'To be unified.',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52'),
(42664,	3784,	5823,	'No.',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52',	'2017-11-13 05:22:52'),
(42665,	4158,	211,	'David never touched Saul after all the opportunities he had\r\nGod pursued David\r\nDavids heart was smitten when he cut Saul\'s robe',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51'),
(42666,	4158,	212,	'You can have God in the desert',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51'),
(42667,	4158,	213,	'none',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51',	'2017-11-12 07:06:51'),
(42668,	260,	9186,	'God likes us to struggle with Him opposite of struggling with God is fleeing from God. Struggling is a face to face with God.\r\nIsrael means struggle with God and also means prince with God. When Jacob struggled with God, it changed his identity.\r\nCARE - Complaint, Appeal, Remind, Express trust',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16'),
(42669,	260,	9187,	'To complaint in faith, and not to complain about God. To complain with declaration of God\'s character, and appeal to His character. To remind God of His promise in His Word.  Expressing trust in God in the end.',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16'),
(42670,	260,	9188,	'It\'s sobering to know that the greatest problem is that we think we are in control, and that is why surrendering is so important and needful when we struggle. Even if we use the approach of CARE, we need to know that we approach God with a intention to surrender to Him, and not to win a debate or accuse Him. I think it\'s a daily active surrender that we do - surrendering of our will, surrendering of our ideals, surrendering of our control.',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16',	'2017-11-13 11:57:16'),
(42671,	281,	9171,	'Where there is growth, there is change and where there is change there is loss, and where there is loss there is pain.\nChange is a part of our lives. We let go of something old to gain something new.\r\nIt is healthy to grief.\nThe fear of our own emotions paralyses us.\r\nYou don’t get over grief, you get through it. \nMaturity is knowing to enter into both the opposites of life.\nComplain to God - worship\nComplain about God - rebellion',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01'),
(42672,	281,	9172,	'Be honest with God about how I am feeling, small or great.',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01'),
(42673,	281,	9173,	'Acknowledging how we feel is an act of humility, all emotions are a gift from God.',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01',	'2017-11-13 15:13:01'),
(42674,	88,	9201,	'I love it when Ptr. Rick Warren shared about Romans 15:4, how the stories in the Bible are meant to give us hope. That was the reason why they were placed there. \r\nIn a sense, it gives me hope that I don\'t have to be perfect and that it is alright to make mistakes and that God will journey with me like he did with the people in the Bible.\r\nKeep on loving in your pain. I agree with what was taught in the sense that I tend to become bitter, hard and unforgiving when I go through something. The challenge is then to allow God to heal you and keep on loving even when something terrible has happened in your life.\r\nWorship expands our vision and gives us spiritual insight.',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37'),
(42675,	88,	9202,	'Worship in the midst of uncertainty and pain. To keep my eyes upon Him even when I face crisis in my life.',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37'),
(42676,	88,	9203,	'On Sunday, Bro Sam talked about \"Breaking imperfection to build connection\". He talked about how our faith statements tend to trip us up when we keep saying that everything is fine and alright in our life. It was in reflection to the sermon yesterday that I can be honest with myself, God and the people around me even when things are bad, I don\'t have to hide, I don\'t have to say: I can\'t believe it. One thing that stood out to me in this video was \"acceptance\" and how it leads eventually to surrender.',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37',	'2017-11-13 15:21:37'),
(42677,	281,	9186,	'The root of all our struggles is our struggle with God\r\nGreatest change happens when our perspectives are exchanged, when we see ourselves differently. Greatest change happens in our identity.\r\nComplain to God (not about God)\nAppeal to God’s character/nature \nRemind God of His promises \nExpress total Trust',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10'),
(42678,	281,	9187,	'Use this acronym of CARE to lament in own life and help others process their struggle',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10'),
(42679,	281,	9188,	'Struggles are a good sign. It means they have not walked away. There is still hope. That gives a new perspective',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10',	'2017-11-13 16:01:10'),
(42680,	4160,	271,	'The purposes of God shaking things... Bring something closer to its foundation, to remove what is dead, to harvest what is right, to awaken, to unify and mix together.\r\nThis is a somewhat under-the-surface point... Revelation knowledge  mixed with unsubmitted, unsurrendered flesh and/or flesh that has not gone through the suffering process becomes the perfect field for Satan to be the angel of light. At the Last Supper there was a dispute among the 12 and they were all thinking only about themselves when Jesus told them that one of them would betray him.\r\nSatan wants to pervert the character of God in our eyes and make us think that God is a taker and not a giver.',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17'),
(42681,	4160,	272,	'It is not in my own ability, it never will be. When I begin to believe and trust in what I can or can\'t do based on what I think I\'m capable of then there is more shaking that needs to be done in me.',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17'),
(42682,	4160,	273,	'When we as a church went through Hurricane Ike and the subsequent trials that followed, it was very much like the storyline of the disciples with Jesus. When things really became difficult many people left and we were faced with the very same question that Jesus asked his core disciples, \"will you leave also?\" To be honest and transparent, we weren\'t sure at that moment what to do. It was a surreal moment and we were torn as to what to do because here were all these people who were ministers, pillars of the church, solid Christians and church leaders. Should we follow these people? What if they\'re right? What if the Glass\'s have some dark secret and we need to get out while we can? Where will we go? What about our family? Who is staying behind? All those questions and many more were going through our minds. The one thing that showed me and was a clear sign that we should stay was when a leading group who were very involved in the music department and other ministries went to Pastor Rich before service and told him they were leaving and their reasons why. I remember it so clearly, Pastor Rich was so crushed and looked so defeated that he told the congregation, those who were left, that he wasn\'t feeling well and Bishop would be preaching. It was seeing him like that in that moment that solidified my course of action. I texted him later that evening that we were staying no matter what happens and no matter who all leaves, God had placed us there and we were not leaving. We were going to stay all the way until they closed the doors for the last time if it came to that and we would do whatever it took to fill in the gaps and keep the church afloat. When your family came you saw us deep in that commitment, were cleaning, maintaining, playing music, singing, helping administratively, etc..  We all were, I\'m speaking of the team. It took that kind of shaking to get us down to our foundation and drew us close together and God could begin bringing into physical existence the vision he had given for this church. In addition to the corporate shaking we all went through a time of personal shaking which further reduced us to the foundation rock and the structure or our personal ministries began to develop and take shape. \n\nLike Andre Crouch sings, \"through it all, I\'ve learned to trust in Jesus, I\'ve learned, I\'ve learned to trust in God.... I\'ve learned to depend upon his word...\"',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17',	'2017-11-13 16:38:17'),
(42683,	88,	9216,	'We really learn to love when God places us around people that are hard to love. It is so easy to love people who are lovable, how about people who are not so lovable.\r\nInstead of asking the question: Why do I have to go through this trial?  \r\nIt would be better to ask: God, what do you want me to learn through this trial?\r\nWe do not give thanks for the pain that we go through, we give thanks in the pain that we go through. We trust that God is able do something through the issues that we go through.',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37'),
(42684,	88,	9217,	'To learn to troubleshoot my trials and ask God what He is trying to teach to me through the trials.',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37'),
(42685,	88,	9218,	'I realize that maturity is a process. Sometimes, I realize that I get into a hurry and get frustrated with God about the whole process but he is like a patient Father drawing me back to His side and encouraging me not to give up. There have been many times this year, that I have had real thoughts on wanting to give up on my role as a care group leader but by the grace of God I have stuck on. This is the case in my relationship with taiyi as well. For me to get corrected by taiyi is not easy, I have had to humble myself but I know that God placed her in my life for His purpose.',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37',	'2017-11-21 19:07:37'),
(42686,	4160,	286,	'Belief = Obedience, Unbelief = Disobedience.  Faith without works is disobedience.\r\nGod uses offense to expose and remove those whom he did not plant.\r\nJesus\' earthly family rejected him at first but later on his mother and brothers were in the upper room.  His own followers and close friends were offended by the truth.',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45'),
(42687,	4160,	287,	'A horse that\'s broken is a horse that\'s submitted. I will continue to fall on the Rock of Offense \"til all my kingdoms fall\".',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45'),
(42688,	4160,	288,	'The truth of God has never been popular.',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45',	'2017-11-13 21:20:45'),
(42689,	4181,	211,	'Harsh Leaders and how they make you stronger.\r\nGentle leaders and how they nurture you.\r\nDavid’s love, even after his harsh leader Saul treated him unfairly. He made him a love song when Saul was killed.',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30'),
(42690,	4181,	212,	'When I get harsh leader or gentle leaders to know that it is a stepping stone to my growth and usually God has put that in my path to grow.',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30'),
(42691,	4181,	213,	'I am greatful to be able to listen to this series, so far it has made me think a bit of things I have gotten offended about before and how I should have a different mind set to it.',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30',	'2017-11-14 18:58:30'),
(42692,	4187,	3571,	'God\'s passion is to bring us into His glory (His full greatness). Moses never got to see God’s glory, in all of the miracles he witnessed.\r\nGod says by those who come near me I MUST be regarded as Holy. There is judgment if He is not regarded as Holy .\r\nGod  is pure light. The light of Jesus \' presence  is so great that Paul couldn\'t even see His face on the road to Damascus. When Jesus returns He will shine so bright that the light of the sun, the stars and the moon will be darkened  because He is so bright with the light of His glory.',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12'),
(42693,	4187,	3572,	'Daily, continuous repentance is so important when it comes to the Glory of God.  Something so simple, but so importance should not be overlooked.  If we desire to see His face and all of His greatness,  we have to keep our lives free from the sin of this world.  When the ground work has been set (repentance) His glory can begin to be evident in our lives.',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12'),
(42694,	4187,	3573,	'When we are baptized with the Holy Ghost we are baptized with fire filling us as He originally desired to be in our hearts( our temple) as with Adam. He is once again dwelling  in His people.',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12',	'2017-11-15 20:13:12'),
(42695,	233,	7386,	'Say goodbye to the demand that someone has to change. Also, say goodbye to the demand that life is fair and just.\r\nLetting go aligns us with \'what is\' and allowing another to make a choice whether to repent. When someone comes back, they will come back for the right reason.\r\nLearn to say what you want and stick with what you want and yet preserve freedom.',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33'),
(42696,	233,	7387,	'I endeavor to let my loved ones have the freedom to choose whether to love me.',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33'),
(42697,	233,	7388,	'Na',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33',	'2017-11-14 09:09:33'),
(42698,	4158,	226,	'How Hannah still submitted her son under Eli even after he being \"The Priest\'  told her she was a drunk while at the Alter pouring her heart out\r\nHow offence hurts but when you give it to God and stay in obedience , He gives you peace in the situation\r\nWhen God is not speaking He is speaking',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26'),
(42699,	4158,	227,	'Leave all in Gods hands',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26'),
(42700,	4158,	228,	'Don\'t pick up the Bait',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26',	'2017-11-14 05:03:26'),
(42701,	3784,	5836,	'Authoratative prayer involves commanding\r\nWe can speak forth what He would have us to say.\r\nThe Lord is above all.',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23'),
(42702,	3784,	5837,	'To pray in authority',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23'),
(42703,	3784,	5838,	'No.',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23',	'2017-11-14 05:29:23'),
(42704,	260,	9201,	'Surrender is the pathway to peace. If we want peace, we need to surrender to God as He pours out blessings in our surrendered attitude. The pain that we go through can help us to love even more deeply.\r\nDo something productive even in grief. I don\'t have to stop mourning to start moving. If I wait till I feel like it I won\'t do anything for a very long time. We should not be paralyze by grief, and mourning can be done while moving. Grieving can happening together with growing. Healing is a choice, a decision we can make.  We do that by surrender.\r\nFind a place that is tranquil and serene to reconnect with God. To see the majesty of God to get that God-perspective.',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45'),
(42705,	260,	9202,	'There are too many important points to absorb and note for this lesson, so one point I want to apply is to listen again and again to internalise the points.',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45'),
(42706,	260,	9203,	'Remember it\'s not the end of the story. It is true, how will God bring beauty from ashes and transit from moving from the present (not being stuck in limbo) to the future. In the long term, we need to think about getting back on track and reconnecting with God. We can do that by taking one small step at a time. King David\'s example is very good.',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45',	'2017-11-16 10:02:45'),
(42707,	3782,	5941,	'We need to loose people who are Timid in church and outside. We can exhort them but it’s better to loose them in the Spirit.\r\nThere are some people we need to turn over to Satan until they learn\r\n\"If she wanted it she would have had it a long time ago\" God withholds nothing good from us.',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32'),
(42708,	3782,	5942,	'I will send confusion to the enemy\'s mind and cover their ears with the blood of Jesus while I speak of  things concerning ministry and other important/ sensitive information.',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32'),
(42709,	3782,	5943,	'Rev shalm is bold in,  and obedient to the Spirit. I told him \"in the name of Jesus shut up and sit down.\"',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32',	'2017-11-14 06:17:32'),
(42710,	169,	9156,	'3 conditions of shock:\r\n1) we know somebody in crisis \r\n2) we are in one right now\r\n3) we do not realise it but we are getting ready going into one!\r\nHelping others in pain or shock and turn into service. Turn it to someone elses salvation, saving grace, hope...\r\nWhen we are in pain, we naturally withdraw (human nature) but it is the opposite if what we need Fellowship, we need people to show up in our life.  The spiritual body lasts longer than the physical body - what happens if the church can really minister to the people in grief/shock /pain properly?',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55'),
(42711,	169,	9157,	'To be able to handle the shocks of life better so that I can help others through them.',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55'),
(42712,	169,	9158,	'Going through second retrenchment, I think I am more\"shock resistant\" but what the author said is true, it is not just going though the pain but it is the God we cry out to that we have help and deliverance from. \r\nThis lesson is so useful, many times we want to help but end up helping wrongly or ineffectively, I like what he presents that when we help we are reducing the stress or effort of the one going through pain to make or take another action that they sometimes cannot or do not have the strength to. Could it be that is the reason why many choose to withdraw not only because of human nature but it is the extra effort they could avoid when in shock/pain',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55',	'2017-11-14 06:43:55'),
(42713,	4158,	241,	'1 Peter 3:13 And who is he who will harm you if you become followers of what is good?\r\nAs Christ sufferers  arm yourself\r\nLetting GOD defend you is the true blessing',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21'),
(42714,	4158,	242,	'Let go and let GOD',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21'),
(42715,	4158,	243,	'none',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21',	'2017-11-14 06:25:21'),
(42716,	4160,	301,	'Truth will offend if one can be offended. God uses this offense to uproot those who he has not planted.\r\nKnowing when to offend and when not to offend is the wisdom of Christ.\r\nWhen one wounds the faith of a weaker believer he sins against Christ.',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19'),
(42717,	4160,	302,	'To bypass my rights and privileges to preserve the faith of my brother and to not cause one to stumble.',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19'),
(42718,	4160,	303,	'Those who preach the Gospel should live by the Gospel being content in poverty and humble in the abundance not \"causing the least of these\" to stumble.',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19',	'2017-11-14 07:17:19'),
(42719,	4160,	316,	'Our forgiveness is to be inexhaustible\r\nForgiveness is releasing those who have hurt us\r\nIf we\'re going to categorize sin then treat gossip as homosexuality.',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47'),
(42720,	4160,	317,	'Not to categorize sin no matter what. Sin is sin. It\'s easy to condemn the murderer while making allowances for the manipulator and thus creating a space for offense to be born. By me being light on manipulation I allow myself to be manipulated and then I\'m hurt, angry, embarrassed and offended and that is difficult to forgive but it\'s my fault because I gave permission to that sin because it did not appear as serious as murder but in the end produced the same exact result.',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47'),
(42721,	4160,	318,	'The above comment will be my reflection for this session.',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47',	'2017-11-14 14:26:47'),
(42722,	233,	7736,	'We should not be distracted  (e.g.. texting, no eye contact) when someone is sharing their issues.\r\nWe should not be interrupting  the conversation and making it about yourself when the other person is speaking.\r\nWe should not appear bored or uninterested by not responding when someone is pouring their heart out.',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35'),
(42723,	233,	7737,	'I have to adopt active listening by repeating what the other party is saying so they know we have understood what they have spoken.',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35'),
(42724,	233,	7738,	'Na',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35',	'2017-11-14 09:18:35'),
(42725,	275,	9186,	'Struggle with (1) Other people (2) Ourselves (3) God\r\nGod loves it when you wrestle with Him. The opposite of struggling with God is walking or running away from God. Wrestling is an intimate sport. \r\n\r\nPattern of Lament:\r\nComplain\r\nAppeal\r\nRemind\r\nTrust\r\n1) Tell God what I think is unfair or painful\r\nComplain to God not about God\r\nComplain in Faith\r\n2) Appeal to God\'s nature\r\n3) Remind God of what He said\r\n4) Express my total trust in God',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25'),
(42726,	275,	9187,	'I found the part on how to Lament very helpful. I am going to apply these principles in prayer.',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25'),
(42727,	275,	9188,	'The portion that said that God likes when we struggle with him. The struggle shows intimacy like how my wife and I would deliberate decisions together and we fight to resolve a situation. \r\n\r\nAlso the portion on how Jacob use to run away whenever he encounters a problem, now he can\'t run but have to face his issues wrestling with God in prayer.',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25',	'2017-11-14 11:21:25'),
(42728,	275,	9201,	'Peace is the emotion that best describes surrender.\r\nSurrendering is accepting reality\r\n\r\n\"What do I need to accept is over in my life?\"\r\n\"I don\'t have to stop mourning to start moving\"',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00'),
(42729,	275,	9202,	'At this moment, I am not able to identify something that I require to apply the steps to peace. But I can apply this lesson by maybe memorizing the 6 steps to peace in surrender right now.',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00'),
(42730,	275,	9203,	'The part that stood out to me was the statement that I do not have to stop mourning to start moving and that baby steps of faith is important to resume life after a loss or grieve. Probably because in movies and even real life, I see how people can hide in a shell and not move on citing the pain they are going through at the moment. While I believe that immediate movement is not possible, but making baby steps is so important otherwise you will never move at all.',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00',	'2017-11-28 10:05:00'),
(42731,	261,	211,	'God sometimes put you in situations where He is trying to test you. To see if you will take matters into your own hands or if you will remain a person after God\'s heart.\r\nIt is one thing to pursue God, but its also another thing to have God pursuing you. Just like how God pursued David. God should always be your first love and not your ministry.\r\nAnything that you go through, God will use it as a stepping stone in your life if you respond in obedience. David realised that the 14 years that he was running from Saul, the persecution that he faced from Saul, was because God was training him to become the shepherd of Israel.',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16'),
(42732,	261,	212,	'Be like David whereby he constantly waited on God and enquired of him. And not like Saul where he took matters into his own hands.',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16'),
(42733,	261,	213,	'Nil',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16',	'2017-11-14 11:49:16'),
(42734,	4160,	331,	'Hebrews 12... I am to examine myself carefully lest there be any root of bitterness...  Either many will be defiled through me or blessed through me.\r\nYou do not avoid offenses, you confront them. Offense must be dealt with.\r\nWaiting for someone to admit that they were wrong is unfulfilled revenge. If Jesus would\'ve waited for us to go to him first to say we\'re sorry and that we were wrong then he never would\'ve gone to the cross.... That one is going to leave a mark, OUCH.',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18'),
(42735,	4160,	332,	'The line \"Father forgive them, they know not what they do\" is all encompassing and so broad that when one lives this as a prayer then there is very little room for offense to try and take root. It makes possible the scriptures such as Colossians 3:13 and Ephesians 4:2 to \" make allowances for each other\".  When I realize that someone may not fully know exactly what they\'re doing or perhaps they may have an unsurrendered area or underdeveloped discipline in their life then I have to make allowances for that. It is immature of me to assume that they are fully mature in all areas of their life. That means that I am setting expectations for them that they will surely fall short of.',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18'),
(42736,	4160,	333,	'I\'ve been so GUILTY of violating what was discussed in this session. This session really cut to the heart deeply. I have been scum, worse that scum, sub-scum.  \"Don\'t resist an evil person that comes to me\"',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18',	'2017-11-14 15:46:18'),
(42737,	4160,	346,	'One can still have a powerful ministry while being in a state of offense and growing colder and colder.  This is very alarming.\r\nPray for those who despitefully wrong me so that what I want for my own life and for my family will be what I ask God for in the lives of those who offend me.\r\nThe goodness of God brought me to repentance.',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23'),
(42738,	4160,	347,	'To exercise my conscience to fervently pray blessings on those who have deeply hurt me.',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23'),
(42739,	4160,	348,	'It\'s my responsibility to create an atmosphere of love, gentleness and kindness so that root of reconciliation can be nurtured rather than continuing to fertilize the roots of bitterness.  I am taking this responsibility seriously. Several years ago God spoke to me and told me that I was going to bring reconciliation to my family that through me healing would come. I had no idea how it was going to happen because it seemed so daunting of a task with the level of difficulty I faced in my near relatives. I am being reminded of it at this moment and I know now that I have to trust God with this and it\'s time to act. I can\'t believe how blind I\'ve been, I\'m embracing God\'s wisdom in this area where I\'ve relied on my own wisdom.',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23',	'2017-11-14 17:23:23'),
(42740,	4149,	181,	'Offense usually starts in the mind.\r\nOnce an offense has happened people tend to build walls to keep everyone out. This plays right into the enemies trap.\r\nPeople tend to be offended most by the people closest to them.',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15'),
(42741,	4149,	182,	'I am excited to learn the tools of offense that Satan uses, so that I can walk through life and be able to identify the early roots of offense.',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15'),
(42742,	4149,	183,	'It is impossible to go through life and not be offended. The Impotant thing is to not allow the offense to grow and be aware of the enemies tactics.',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15',	'2017-11-14 18:29:15'),
(42743,	4149,	196,	'God’s will can not be stopped by anyone except for yourself.\r\nSpreading and gossiping about offense is just a bad as offending someone yourself.\r\nGod’s word will always come to pass as long as we do not get offended and complain.',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21'),
(42744,	4149,	197,	'I pray that God will give me a fresh perspective to see ,with His vision, the offenses that come to me. We have to see the purpose behind the offense and submit to God’s process.',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21'),
(42745,	4149,	198,	'God allows things to happen to us in order to build the necessary character to handle to responsibility He has called us to. We must submit to the process and allow God’s will to be done in our lives.',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21',	'2017-11-14 19:42:21'),
(42746,	4149,	211,	'All leaders are ordained by God. No matter if they are harsh or gentle, they are still chosen by God.\r\nHow you choose to deal with an offense will determine the course of your future.\r\nSometimes God uses offenses to test our character.',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19'),
(42747,	4149,	212,	'In every process that God allows you to experience, He either wants to put something in you or take something out. I want to get to a place where I am fully submitted to the process and understand that God is trying to implement a tool to my life.',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19'),
(42748,	4149,	213,	'When a person lives for God, there aren’t any coincidences. Everything has a purpose and lesson for you to learn from. Offenses are the same way. God can use the ugliest, most hurtful things to create a beautiful testimony for your life.',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19',	'2017-11-14 21:03:19'),
(42749,	4149,	226,	'When you get offended it typically is a reflection of the immaturity in your life.\r\nAdversity is placed to cause you to go deeper and hold onto the things of God.\r\nOffense is the doorway to a sinful life.',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08'),
(42750,	4149,	227,	'I want to look at adversity, not as punishment, but as something that is making me stronger. God will not allow offense and trials to destroy me, but He will use them to push me to dig deeper within myself and in Him. God desires for our faith to grow through everything, including offense.',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08'),
(42751,	4149,	228,	'If you are rooted and firmly planted in God’s will and plan, He will give you the endurance to stand up against your adversities. God allows the winds of life to blow to increase your faith and trust in Him. This happens so that  when hard times come you will be able to withstand the trial.',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08',	'2017-11-14 22:59:08'),
(42752,	4149,	241,	'Kingdom living will keep you from offense.\r\nMost of the people in churches today are not armed for suffering which is why they are so easily offended.\r\nThe church as a whole needs to stop reacting and start acting when offense comes.',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20'),
(42753,	4149,	242,	'When an offense or trial comes into my life, I want to look at if from the perspective of expectancy. When these thing emerged my life I know that God is stretching me and causing me grow deeper in Him. I no longer want to view them from a defeated outlook, but from an excited one.',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20'),
(42754,	4149,	243,	'The true sign of spiritual growth is when you you can come in contact with offense and not be offended by it. Until you are able to not react to the same offense time and time again, you will have to repeat the lesson. You only grow deeper when the same trivial things stop affecting you.',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20',	'2017-11-15 00:23:20'),
(42755,	4149,	256,	'Revelation happens when an atmosphere of hunger is developed.\r\nPrayer has to be a conversation not repeating something memorized.\r\nJust like the church body is supposed to pray without ceasing, God desires to be continuously speak to us. We just have to be quiet enough to listen.',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09'),
(42756,	4149,	257,	'I never want to loose my zeal for growing deeper in the Lord. If I loose my hunger I will become stagnant and become more susceptible to the offense the enemy puts in my path. My desire for God and His presence has to outweigh my carnal flesh. That is the only way to live life without offense.',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09'),
(42757,	4149,	258,	'We must have a revelation for ourselves. If we do not have a personal relationship with the Almighty and understand  who He truly is, we will become shallow and empty spiritually. If we are shallow and do not have a firm grip on the truth, we will not have enough backbone to withstand when adversity attacks us.',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09',	'2017-11-15 01:24:09'),
(42758,	4183,	196,	'No matter what keep the fear of God ( stay obedient)\r\nGossip is  Abomination to God\r\noffense brings betrayal',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27'),
(42759,	4183,	197,	'Maintain the fear of God because I do not want to interfere with God\'s will',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27'),
(42760,	4183,	198,	'When going through battles always remember the greatest attacks come. Right before the harvest',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27',	'2017-11-15 01:31:27'),
(42761,	4160,	1,	'Those who do not understand God do not understand authority\r\nMany resist the authority of God by claiming they have only God as their spiritual authority. Whether it\'s God\'s direct authority or delegated authority, it\'s still authority given by God and to resist any part of it is to rebel against God and His authority.\r\nHis testimony about the giant youth program and the \"parties\", the home fellowships is amazing! And his rebellion following the decision of his senior pastor...   God puts one man over a ministry.  Division = two visions.  This is deep stuff.',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26'),
(42762,	4160,	2,	'To be faithful to the spiritual authority that I have been placed under, only one vision. God forbid that I should birth an Ishmael out of rebellion.',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26'),
(42763,	4160,	3,	'I\'m reflecting',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26',	'2017-11-15 05:14:26'),
(42764,	3784,	5851,	'Satan tried to destroy man, Gods favorite creation.\r\nThe Holy Ghost moves when we pray.\r\nPrayer removes the demonic or negative influence of a person which in turn allows the Holy ghost to influence.',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37'),
(42765,	3784,	5852,	'Pray authoritative prayers.',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37'),
(42766,	3784,	5853,	'No.',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37',	'2017-11-15 05:23:37'),
(42767,	3784,	5866,	'Never argue or compromise with an evil spirit, COMMAND.\r\nDont fear the Devil\r\nPosture speaks volumes',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13'),
(42768,	3784,	5867,	'Stand in Victory',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13'),
(42769,	3784,	5868,	'No',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13',	'2017-11-15 05:52:13'),
(42770,	3784,	5881,	'The head of satan is under our heel.\r\nWe are passing through, this is not our home.\r\nRise up in the authority of theHoly Ghost and fight.',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43'),
(42771,	3784,	5882,	'Use my Authority in Christ to set the captives free.',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43'),
(42772,	3784,	5883,	'No.',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43',	'2017-11-15 06:33:43'),
(42773,	3784,	5896,	'General prayers get general answers Specific prayers get specific answers.\r\nHumility will allow the Lord to hear you.\r\nPersistence ...',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34'),
(42774,	3784,	5897,	'To pray in authority.',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34'),
(42775,	3784,	5898,	'No.',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34',	'2017-11-15 07:11:34'),
(42776,	4015,	7326,	'Loving people have no fear because they\'re free.\r\nLoving people can heal better from wounds.\r\nthe more you love, the greater your capacity to love others.',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11'),
(42777,	4015,	7327,	'To love those others consider unlovable.',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11'),
(42778,	4015,	7328,	'nobody can really love unless they\'ve been loved',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11',	'2017-11-15 07:19:11'),
(42779,	3784,	5911,	'If we pray Authoratative prayers we must submit tho those in authority above us.\r\nThere is a proper way to fast. And a wrong way to fast.\r\nFasting and prayer go hand in hand.',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12'),
(42780,	3784,	5912,	'Fast more.',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12'),
(42781,	3784,	5913,	'No.',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12',	'2017-11-15 07:46:12'),
(42782,	4183,	211,	'Often the thing that looks like an abortion to God\'s plan is what leads to the road of his work if we stay obedient and free of offense\r\nWe we must go through the Wilderness through the fire of referring to be to handle leadership position\r\nAnything we go through God will use it to as a stepping stone if we respond in obedience',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46'),
(42783,	4183,	212,	'Still beating you even through all all of my hardships',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46'),
(42784,	4183,	213,	'Respond in obedience no matter when or what I\'m going through',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46',	'2017-11-15 08:03:46'),
(42785,	3784,	5926,	'A church must have prayer warriors to overcome.\r\nYou cannot be an overcomer without being a prayer warrior.\r\nAuthoratative prayer is  commanding instead of asking God underatandong it is His will. Get your prayer in the right direction. Use His authority to deal with problems on his behalf.\r\nWeaknesses are anger unclean thoughts that become mountains in our lives. Speak to the situation specifically. Remove and Bind in the name of Jesus.',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08'),
(42786,	3784,	5927,	'Have authorative prayers.',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08'),
(42787,	3784,	5928,	'No.',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08',	'2017-11-29 04:48:08'),
(42788,	233,	7751,	'We can show care and love by paying attention to others.\r\nWe have to let others feel safe, letting others process their issues and responding to statement has been spoken.\r\nIt takes courage to name the issue in the small group even though  you will make the group feel uncomfortable.',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46'),
(42789,	233,	7752,	'I endeavor to create a safe environment for by care group members to share their issues.',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46'),
(42790,	233,	7753,	'Na',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46',	'2017-11-15 08:42:46'),
(42791,	4160,	16,	'There is a power of lawlessness\r\nBeing thankful keeps our focus on everything God has given us rather than the one thing he commanded us not to \'eat\'.\r\nHumanity has substituted obedience with the principle of reasoning',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25'),
(42792,	4160,	17,	'To stand strong and not let the world, human reasoning, my own intellect or the devil to pervert the character of God in my eyes.',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25'),
(42793,	4160,	18,	'The greatest and most subtle temptation is \"if you are the song of God\"...  That tiny word \"if\" from Satan which he places as the first word of his question is very cunning and powerful and if we\'re not in love with truth, wholely submitted to God and in obedience to His will; that \"if\" will get us.',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25',	'2017-11-15 15:59:25'),
(42794,	4160,	31,	'If you are ever going to be submitted to God\'s authority, you must have a revelation of who Jesus is\r\n\"Offering\" speaks of life service to God\r\nSin has a desire whether Satan is present or not. It permeates everything and only obedience to God will protect us. The law of sin and death is always in effect so I must live according to the Law of the Spirit of Life in Christ Jesus through obedience to Him.',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16'),
(42795,	4160,	32,	'Faith and obedient actions are directly connected.',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16'),
(42796,	4160,	33,	'Grace empowers us to live according to the Law of the Spirit and to walk in obedience. Grace is not the great cover up of my selfish desires and fleshly actions based on my reasoning. Grace is the power to serve God in a way He sees as acceptable.',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16',	'2017-11-15 16:37:16'),
(42797,	4205,	1,	'Being under authority gives protection and provision over your life\r\nWe are the extension of our Pastors hands\r\nWe must seek the heart of God when reading the Word of God',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11'),
(42798,	4205,	2,	'to strive to better understand and to always be submitted to God\'s authority.',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11'),
(42799,	4205,	3,	'I found it interesting when he talked about division = two visions\r\nI always want to make sure to have the God\'s vision and not my own.',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11',	'2017-11-15 19:22:11'),
(42800,	4204,	1,	'Adam and Eve tried to find an alternate covering when they came from under their authority.\r\nDeceived people like to bring God to their level so they can teach God what he should be doing.\r\nYou can be doing all the right things (ministry), think you’re doing the will of God and not be submitted.  Thinking you’re right with God doesn’t mean you’re submitted and covered.',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12'),
(42801,	4204,	2,	'I will endeavor to be broken and repentant before God of any rebellion.',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12'),
(42802,	4204,	3,	'My boss at work has been someone who is retired while working.  I’ve been filled with frustration over his lack of caring, and had been pushing back with my comments toward him.  However, I don’t have peace to leave the organization, and feel God is trying to teach me something about being humbly submitted under his authority even though he isn’t doing what is right.  I’ve already started to see a change in myself and my boss as I’ve adjusted my attitude and actions.',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12',	'2017-11-17 03:55:12'),
(42803,	3800,	1021,	'--The spirit will not always lead you because, when your flesh gets involved, the flesh rises and the spirit lowers. My flesh will begin to rise when I court.-- It\'s just something that will happen.\r\n-Guidelines need to be set in courting, to prevent loosing control. Limits must be set, once limits are set, our conscience will kick in.\r\n--Levels of friendships:\r\n1. Acquaintance: you will find out if its a wholesome friendship or a unwholesome friendship. -- Occasional contact, general questions (public info). Wanna have friends? Be friendly. \r\n2. Casual friend: (Specific information, positive character qualities.)',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49'),
(42804,	3800,	1022,	'--What I do now, will have a 100% effect on my marriage. --The habits you do in your courting years will following into your marriage years.',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49'),
(42805,	3800,	1023,	'--What\'s the reason for not courting until your 21?',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49',	'2017-11-16 23:54:49'),
(42806,	4015,	7341,	'Things that get transferred in connection: feelings, desires, fears, failures and hurts, and God\r\nTo be a connector, you cannot be afraid of discussing/dealing with failures, loss, and pain.\r\nIt\'s important that you don\'t look at someone as a project, but you love them just as they are.',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53'),
(42807,	4015,	7342,	'Learn to suspend my point of view to see how the other person feels.',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53'),
(42808,	4015,	7343,	'When trying to connect with someone, its important not to just give them advice, but to listen',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53',	'2017-11-16 07:42:53'),
(42809,	3799,	1021,	'during acquaintance period you will find out if it is wholesome or not.\r\nif you are not careful it is easy to let the flesh rise.\r\nDating has become so casual, and it is just to taste and try other things. dating is not courting.',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34'),
(42810,	3799,	1022,	'to learn and apply the levels of friendships.',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34'),
(42811,	3799,	1023,	'I just thought it was crazy how i didn\'t realize the differences between dating at courting! defiantly something i need to work on.',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34',	'2017-11-17 01:00:34'),
(42812,	4200,	181,	'It is impossible that offense should not come but it is up to us how we respond to it.\r\nThe life (the good news) we receive we should give out (tell others) otherwise it will die within us.\r\nOffense is the breeding ground for deception',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48'),
(42813,	4200,	182,	'The breaking down of strongholds in my life',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48'),
(42814,	4200,	183,	'This truly applies to me because i have been offended in the past and it has made me unable to trust others. I realize now that to love unconditionally gives others the right to hurt you.  It\'s the will of God that we love unconditionally any way.',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48',	'2017-11-16 09:14:48'),
(42815,	260,	9216,	'God teaches us a fruit of the spirit by placing us in the exact opposite of the quality that He wants us to have. For example, God wants us to have joy by placing us in moments of sadness.\r\nGod uses problems, pressure and pain to make us to be more like Him. 2 Cor 4:8-9. Every problem has a purpose. We are transformed by our troubles.\r\nBeing a Christian doesn\'t mean being trouble-free. In fact, we should expect trouble as it is written in His word and also because God uses trouble to make us more Christ-like.',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16'),
(42816,	260,	9217,	'Do the 3 things described in the sermon -  1. Remember that God\'s plan is good. 2. Rejoice and give thanks in everything, for this is the will of God. 3. Refuse to give up.',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16'),
(42817,	260,	9218,	'Having questions are sometimes more important than having the answers. I thought the way he ended with the following questions is quite thought-provoking and a good way to frame our perspective in light of pain and suffering - \"What do you want me to learn? How can I be more like you through this?\"',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16',	'2017-11-16 10:53:16'),
(42818,	273,	9171,	'If I don\'t let it out in healthy ways, i\'m going to act it out in unhealthy ways.\r\nRevealing your feeling is the beginning of healing.\r\nYou don\'t get over grief, you get through it.',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33'),
(42819,	273,	9172,	'To list down/identify my losses that I have never grieved.',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33'),
(42820,	273,	9173,	'I\'ve come to realise how the things I\'ve failed to grieve for, have become subconsciously become a source of frustration/bitterness.',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33',	'2017-11-16 12:47:33'),
(42821,	273,	9186,	'God loves it when we struggle with Him.\r\nC - Complain\r\nA - Appeal to God’s Nature/Character\r\nR - Remind God of His Promises/Reputation\r\nE - Express Trust in God’s Wisdom\r\nI need to tell God what I think is unfair or painful.',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34'),
(42822,	273,	9187,	'Not to sweep things under the rug & pretend like nothing is wrong, learn to struggle with God.',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34'),
(42823,	273,	9188,	'Honestly, I\'m not too sure how much I\'ve truly struggled with God…makes me wonder how much running away have I done through my life.',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34',	'2017-11-16 13:25:34'),
(42824,	273,	9201,	'Acceptance just means I can\'t change the outcome.\r\nI don\'t have to stop mourning to start moving.\r\nJesus kept on loving through pain; His act on the cross.',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40'),
(42825,	273,	9202,	'Learn to be productive in the process of grieving, because it is so easy to slip into the idea of just wallowing in emotions & not do anything productive.',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40'),
(42826,	273,	9203,	'Remember it is not the end due to a major negative outcome, it could just be the beginning of something else more beneficial.',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40',	'2017-11-16 14:01:40'),
(42827,	4200,	196,	'Cut off the gossipers\r\nCritical-ness is the counter part to discernment\r\nGod uses our bad choices to transform our lives for good',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43'),
(42828,	4200,	197,	'Cut off the gossipers',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43'),
(42829,	4200,	198,	'Every decision i have made in my life has lead me to this place. God has used those decisions and his will to mold me',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43',	'2017-11-16 15:02:43'),
(42830,	4160,	46,	'When I believes they can serve God through their rebellion then I  am in big trouble.\r\nThe goal of witchcraft is to control... \"Do what thou will\"\r\nThere is no witchcraft against the church nor is there any divination against God\'s people.   \n\"Like a fluttering sparrow or a darting swallow, an undeserved curse will not land on its intended victim.\" Proverbs 26:2 NLT',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11'),
(42831,	4160,	47,	'To walk in and communicate to others the principle of No Curses. In the words of Balaam: \" how can one curse those whom God has not cursed\"?  In obedience is the safety.',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11'),
(42832,	4160,	48,	'None',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11',	'2017-11-16 15:24:11'),
(42833,	4157,	181,	'One point that stood out to me was the expectations we place on other people and how this causes us to be offended when they don\'t meet up to our expectations.\r\nAnother point that stood out to me is  when we\'re completely embraced by the love of God we\'re giving love  and there\'s no second thought  but as soon as we get hurt / offended our walls go up and we start protecting instead of giving.\r\nThe third point that stood out to me it\'s how God is love. How his love for us is agape, unconditional and the only ones who can love with the same love as God are those who have  received the Holy Spirit. That the strongest force in the universe is God, who is love!',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04'),
(42834,	4157,	182,	'All three. I plan to forgive more quickly and lower my expectations of those around me. I plan to spend more time with Jesus so He can fill me up with His love and I will freely give what He has given me. I will depend on Jesus to help me overcome offense when it comes.',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04'),
(42835,	4157,	183,	'Before this lesson I didn\'t realize that my older children have offended me by not meeting the expectations I had placed on them. The Lord Jesus  is helping me forgive them and lower my expectations of them.',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04',	'2017-11-17 15:09:04'),
(42836,	4200,	211,	'As long as we are free from the bitterness of offense and we trust the Lord nothing can keep us from his purpose for our lives\r\nThe harsh leader is used by God to refine us\r\nIt\'s not my job to correct those God has appointed to lead me. That is the Lord\'s  job',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02'),
(42837,	4200,	212,	'Appreciate the harsh leaders in my life',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02'),
(42838,	4200,	213,	'I\'ve seen this in my life where I\'ve had a leader that was tough towards me but In the end it made me a stronger person',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02',	'2017-11-16 16:19:02'),
(42839,	4200,	226,	'An offended person feels like everyone is out to get them\r\nWe must be rooted in our church in order to flourish\r\nWe don\'t choose the church we attend God has already decided that for us',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07'),
(42840,	4200,	227,	'I want to have deep roots',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07'),
(42841,	4200,	228,	'I\'ve moved from job to job due to offense,so i see the truth in this!',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07',	'2017-11-16 17:01:07'),
(42842,	4200,	241,	'1 Peter 3:8 is the formula to not be offended\r\nSpiritual growth is a function of suffering\r\nRejoice when you suffer',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20'),
(42843,	4200,	242,	'Do not repay evil for evil',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20'),
(42844,	4200,	243,	'The next time I endure suffering I\'m going to thank God because I\'ll  know it\'s an opportunity  to  grow and show maturity',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20',	'2017-11-16 17:54:20'),
(42845,	4205,	16,	'ANYTHING that becomes more important than INSTANTLY obeying the WORD of GOD is sin.\r\ndeception = you really believe that you\'re right when you\'re wrong\r\nmankind has substituted the principle of obedience for the principle of reasoning',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10'),
(42846,	4205,	17,	'loving truth = loving to obey truth\r\n\r\nfinding a new love and desire for truth over all so that deception cannot come into my life.',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10'),
(42847,	4205,	18,	'one other point that stood out to me is .......When a person hears the Word of God but does not do it deception enters the heart.....\r\nI want to do what the Word of God has instructed me to do and I want to be able to show others practical ways to do what the Word of God is instructing.',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10',	'2017-11-16 18:10:10'),
(42848,	4200,	256,	'When God reveals something to you no one can take that from you\r\nWhen we pray without ceasing God communicates without ceasing\r\nHave an appetite for God and revelation knowledge will abound',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17'),
(42849,	4200,	257,	'Prayer is a dialogue, listen out for God as he speaks',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17'),
(42850,	4200,	258,	'I sometimes find my self in prayer talking God\'s ear off but never listening to what he has to say. I should listen more',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17',	'2017-11-16 18:44:17'),
(42851,	4200,	271,	'God shakes us to improve us. To sift out all the bad so that only his goodness remains\r\nA strong spirit is revealed through the pressure of life\r\nThe revelation of knowing who Jesus is keeps you going',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11'),
(42852,	4200,	272,	'Be rooted in the love of God',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11'),
(42853,	4200,	273,	'There is nothing good for me outside of God\'s will for me',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11',	'2017-11-16 19:31:11'),
(42854,	242,	9186,	'Our biggest battle is with our fears, flaws, temptations, insecurities, guilt, regret, resentment, compulsions, weaknesses, addictions, sins\r\nWe struggle with other people\r\n1. Every r/s is broken by sin\r\n2. Because nothing works perfectly we have competition, conflicts, we have misunderstandings, disappointments\r\n3. Jacob\'s life demonstrates the \"normality\" of struggle – struggled with Esau (his brother), Leah & Rachel (wives), in-laws, 12 sons, it was a very dysfunctional family (the Bible has dysfunctional families, I\'m in good company haha)\r\nHow to lament to God\r\nC omplain (God, why don’t You do ___? God when are You going to answer my prayer?)\r\nA ppeal (to God’s nature/character/attributes)\r\nR emind (of His promises, reputation, truth, what He said)\r\nE xpress trust in God’s wisdom',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14'),
(42855,	242,	9187,	'Wrestling with God to win\r\n1. Tell God what I think is unfair or painful\r\n2. Appeal to God’s nature\r\n3. Remind God of what He has said \r\n4. Express our total trust in God\r\n\r\nLord, I trust You with this, I trust Your goodness, I trust Your wisdom, I trust Your love, even in the bad things that happen that I don’t understand',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14'),
(42856,	242,	9188,	'This part that Pastor Warren shared, spoke to me:\r\n\r\nGod does His deepest work in your life in YOUR IDENTITY – when He can change the way you see yourself it changes you – anything you want to change in your life, it starts with change in perspective – until God changes the way you see yourself, nothing much is going to happen in your life, you will struggle the rest of your life.\r\n\r\nMy reflections:\r\n\r\nIn my pride & \"fixer\" mentality, I kept thinking that I didn\'t need to talk out my struggle with people because there were no issues that the people could immediately help me fix. This is not the first time I have thought this, so it’s a stronghold I have to address.\r\n\r\nAs I started digesting the first lesson of this Grief series, about not isolating, I knew the right thing to do was to talk to people who cared & could support me even when I may not have been ready to receive their support. It was hard humbling myself to be vulnerable with my thoughts & emotions. Frustrating because I had not accepted the necessary part of life where we wrestle, and also slightly reassuring, knowing that I had space to be honest & break down my own image of perfection that I had spent years building up & hiding behind. \r\n\r\nThis is new for me. I’m still digesting it.',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14',	'2017-11-30 13:59:14'),
(42857,	4192,	1,	'Resisting those that are in authority in my life is resisting God. God does things out of love and not out of legalism.\r\nStudents were able to win other students to God by inviting them to small groups known as parties. I appreciate their method of doing that. They would get their numbers, call them on Monday and have them at the “party” on Wednesday.\r\nIt stuck with me how two 14 year olds would pray from 4:00 am to 8:00 am and them they would go to school. That’s dedication.',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11'),
(42858,	4192,	2,	'I will endeavor to apply prayer for patience in my life so that I will accept the authority that has been placed over me.',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11'),
(42859,	4192,	3,	'Hopefully I will be one of those that will dwell in that secret place in the presence of the Almighty God.',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11',	'2017-11-17 06:01:11'),
(42860,	4205,	31,	'to do well with God is to obey him\r\nthe highest form of worship is obedience\r\nwhen someone allows disobedience in their life they bring God to their level (lower the image of God, they think they know more or better than God)',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47'),
(42861,	4205,	32,	'to make sure I am living a God-conscious and not a self-conscious life.',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47'),
(42862,	4205,	33,	'Grace empowers us to do what truth demands of us!!!!! This statement almost at the very end of the lesson really stuck out to me.',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47',	'2017-11-17 17:09:47'),
(42863,	4183,	226,	'All authority is appointed by God respect them but only obey them if it\'s not deliberately against God\'s will\r\nAdversity deepens roots if you if we allow the Holy Spirit to work in US during adversity we will become sweeter in our fruit\r\nWhen looking for change or an answer to a problem and God doesn\'t speak or give us any type of sign he is telling us not to make a change',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46'),
(42864,	4183,	227,	'When faced with adversity I will let the Holy Spirit work in me that I may become deep deeply rooted and strengthen my walk with God',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46'),
(42865,	4183,	228,	'The day I got saved I was told to go to the church triumphant buy two brothers in Christ but now I know it wasn\'t them telling me it was a spirit letting me know that this will be my home Church',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46',	'2017-11-17 04:59:46'),
(42866,	4200,	286,	'Belief is to obey\r\nChrist is the rock of offense, the sword of truth\r\nGOd will use offense to drive people out that aren\'t working in his kingdom',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52'),
(42867,	4200,	287,	'I will obey the commands of the Lord because that is belief',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52'),
(42868,	4200,	288,	'It makes sense that the world would be offended by the truth of God and why Christians are still persecuted because the truth we tell is so offensive to the world because it is the truth of Jesus the rock of offense',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52',	'2017-11-17 05:29:52'),
(42869,	4200,	301,	'A slave has to serve a servant gets to serve\r\nWe should use our privelage to serve one another\r\nWe take care not to offend so that we do not cause a brother to stumble',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08'),
(42870,	4200,	302,	'I will serve my brother and do my best not to offend so that he may not stumble',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08'),
(42871,	4200,	303,	'It\'s scary to think that I could offend someone to the point that their faith falters',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08',	'2017-11-17 06:09:08'),
(42872,	4200,	316,	'All sin is sin there is no better or worse\r\nIf we do not forgive God will not forgive us\r\nWe have the ability to forgive as he forgives you',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09'),
(42873,	4200,	317,	'Forgiveness sets us free and keeps us right with God',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09'),
(42874,	4200,	318,	'Forgiveness is a powerful thing',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09',	'2017-11-17 06:54:09'),
(42875,	4200,	331,	'You have to deal with offenses\r\nDo not repay evil for evil\r\nDon\'t defile yourself with revenge or bitterness',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45'),
(42876,	4200,	332,	'Vengeance and judgement belong to the Lord alone',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45'),
(42877,	4200,	333,	'It\'s easy to try to take matters into our own hands but that doesn\'t leave room for God to work in our lives. In the end God judges all.',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45',	'2017-11-17 07:59:45'),
(42878,	4200,	346,	'There is a difference between forgiveness and reconciliation\r\nWe should pray for our brother who has offended us so that we do not build a wall between ourselves and God\r\nWe have to create an atmosphere thats full of love and goodness when we go to our brother',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53'),
(42879,	4200,	347,	'Excercise. In prayer, fasting and studying the word',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53'),
(42880,	4200,	348,	'Ive definately been offended. There are brothers and sisters who I still harbor hurt feelings against but this has helped me to repent and change my heart! Thank you Jesus!',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53',	'2017-11-18 16:35:53'),
(42881,	4015,	7356,	'Truth brings resources: advice, suggestion, wisdom.\r\nYou must integrate love with truth.\r\nAffirming people aren\'t always a good thing.',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11'),
(42882,	4015,	7357,	'To make sure i know my motives behind telling the truth.',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11'),
(42883,	4015,	7358,	'telling the truth can help people to grow',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11',	'2017-11-17 09:49:11'),
(42884,	4157,	196,	'One point that stood out to me is true discernment is rooted in the love of God and to know if we are really discerning someone amd not being critical, we must ask ourselves if we will die for them.\r\nThe next point is God will protect a persons right to go to hell if they want to go to hell.\r\nThe third point is to feed on Gods faithfulness when life gets  tough. Also how no one or nothing can destroy the will of God on my life but me.',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06'),
(42885,	4157,	197,	'A point I plan to apply in my life is to not complain and  keep seeking what true discernment means and looks like in my life. I want to love like Jesus 100%. And His will to be accomplished in my life.',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06'),
(42886,	4157,	198,	'I desire more wisdom on how God will protect a persons right to go to hell if he chooses to go to hell. I am under the impression that this is referring to our free will.',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06',	'2017-11-21 05:07:06'),
(42887,	4179,	1,	'If I take myself out from under authority, I have rebelled against God himself.\r\nThere is no legitimate authority outside of God.\r\nGod set up authorities in our homes, in church, and in society out of love.',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58'),
(42888,	4179,	2,	'To avoid resisting authority or to kick against the goads...',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58'),
(42889,	4179,	3,	'Excellent teaching.',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58',	'2017-11-17 16:57:58'),
(42890,	4205,	46,	'religious spirit  = one who uses God\'s word to execute their own desires\r\nGod works in a 3 step process to get your attention\r\nconscience, messenger, judgement\r\nradical obedience stops the curse of radical disobedience',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36'),
(42891,	4205,	47,	'making sure there are no areas in my life where I am partially obedient to God',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36'),
(42892,	4205,	48,	'I have personally seen the consequences of disobedience destroy an entire church and family.  The whole family was brought under witchcraft.  It is a very hard thing to watch even from the outside but I am praying that someones radical obedience can turn things around for the people who are still being effected by this.',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36',	'2017-11-17 18:56:36'),
(42893,	4187,	3586,	'God is in a secret place,  but He welcomes in those who fear the Lord.\r\nGreater the glory,  greater the judgment. The reason  that we don\'t  see judgment  today like we read in the book of Acts is the level  of  the glory of God is not as great as it was then today.\r\nGiving is a gift . Jesus kept a close eye on those who gave . Giving has to be done for the right reason or judgment will occur.',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41'),
(42894,	4187,	3587,	'Sacrifice has to be combined with fear of the Lord.',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41'),
(42895,	4187,	3588,	'N/A',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41',	'2017-11-22 22:41:41'),
(42896,	4205,	61,	'kingdom authority \r\n-protection\r\n-provision\r\n-His presence\r\nGod\'s first priority is not our comfort, it is redemption\r\nGod know whom he appoints; because he plans it......\r\nGod always has a plan',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00'),
(42897,	4205,	62,	'If you know God, you will know His authority -- I want to make sure this is evident in my life',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00'),
(42898,	4205,	63,	'I want to be an example to those around me by living under the authority of God with a great spirit and attitude.',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00',	'2017-11-18 18:07:00'),
(42899,	4218,	1,	'rebellion is idolitary\r\nits important to be submitted to the man of God that God placed over you\r\nthere is freedom in obeying God\'s Word',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19'),
(42900,	4218,	2,	'i will make up my mind to be more supportive and submitted to the men of God that is placed in my life',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19'),
(42901,	4218,	3,	'very convicting...',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19',	'2017-11-18 00:44:19'),
(42902,	4218,	16,	'sin is lawlessness\r\ni can still be in the church,but still be in sin by doing things my way\r\njust because i think it\'s right don\'t mean its right. there is nothing right outside the will of God...',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12'),
(42903,	4218,	17,	'be more aware of God\'s Word and seek to do his will more.',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12'),
(42904,	4218,	18,	'very convicting',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12',	'2017-11-18 01:37:12'),
(42905,	4236,	1,	'Submission\r\nPower\r\nLiberty',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43'),
(42906,	4236,	2,	'To be sensitive in the Holy Spirit to being submitted to authority',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43'),
(42907,	4236,	3,	'No',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43',	'2017-11-18 04:50:43'),
(42908,	4206,	1,	'The need to be under authority to the extent of changing when directed to, even when you are sure you are doing what God said to do.\r\nYou can be doing all the \"things\" you\'re supposed to be and still be in rebellion\r\nWhat God is doing to reach people with one group may have no relationship to what he is doing with another.',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01'),
(42909,	4206,	2,	'Keep being in obedience to authority',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01'),
(42910,	4206,	3,	'No',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01',	'2017-11-18 04:51:01'),
(42911,	4203,	1,	'One must stay under divine authority\r\nAuthority is protection\r\nto know God intimately',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25'),
(42912,	4203,	2,	'to know God intimately',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25'),
(42913,	4203,	3,	'Desire a passion to live in submission and authority.',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25',	'2017-11-18 05:46:25'),
(42914,	4202,	1,	'Authority\r\nInseparable\r\nSeeking Gods heart',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40'),
(42915,	4202,	2,	'Staying under authority',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40'),
(42916,	4202,	3,	'Strive to apply the word to your life',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40',	'2017-11-18 06:23:40'),
(42917,	3828,	5911,	'God\'s army has a chain of command and the lines of authority need to be clearly understood. There are no independent soldiers in man\'s army, not even the snipers work alone they have spotters. Good soldiers take commands and submit to the authority over them. Soldiers work as a team, and God\'s soldiers never die, we multiply.\r\nPrayer is my connection with the Commander. Prayer is the only real way for me to show God my desire to know him intimately. Prayer that goes beyond just telling God all my troubles. Prayer that  touches the heart of my Commander where He will trust me, His faithful servant, to do His will and follow His commands.\r\nFasting is the key to a breakthrough. Fasting is a physical illustration of self-denial where one can surrender his will to that of God\'s will. Fasting is the way we deny ourselves our God given right to eat, be full and satisfied. But what good of it if we boost or desire for all to know that we are fasting. It is best we wash our face and let our sacrifice be known only by God.',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53'),
(42918,	3828,	5912,	'Increase my prayer life and train myself for times of fasting that I might break through in the Spirit to reach a new level of knowing God.',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53'),
(42919,	3828,	5913,	'Question #4 puzzled me because I couldn\'t find a definitive one word answer. \"Commandments,\" perhaps? However, what I gathered in whole is we must also submit to His will, commandments, and those in authority over us, spiritual or otherwise.',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53',	'2017-11-18 06:43:53'),
(42920,	273,	9216,	'Though our bodies are dying, our spirits are being renewed.\r\nNot all things on earth are good, but God can make everything to work together for good.\r\n(1) Remember God\'s plan is good\r\n(2) Rejoice & give thanks (even in pain, not for it)\r\n(3) Refuse to give up',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53'),
(42921,	273,	9217,	'Assess my problems, so that I can glean any lesson & be more self-awareness.',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53'),
(42922,	273,	9218,	'I think the point on rejoicing through it, not for it was an slight eye-opener...cause its easy to fall into the misconception that I should always thank God for the trials/pain.',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53',	'2017-11-18 12:35:53'),
(42923,	273,	9231,	'That there are treasures (concealed riches) hidden in (the suffering of) darkness for us to find.\r\nWhat we know leads us to worship.\r\nThe idea of hanging/anchoring my soul, so that it would led by emotions or be caught up with the flow.',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03'),
(42924,	273,	9232,	'To identify & memorize scriptures that will aid to anchor my soul, the go-to scriptures that keep me grounded.',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03'),
(42925,	273,	9233,	'Even though I don\'t think i am in a season of darkness, this lesson was sobering & kinda helps me watch out for things that I might be in danger of doing.',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03',	'2017-11-18 13:19:03'),
(42926,	273,	9246,	'5 Purposes in Life\r\n•	Worship - Learn to love God\r\n•	Fellowship - Love to love others\r\n•	Discipleship - Become like Christ\r\n•	Ministry - Serve God by Serving Other People\r\n•	Mission - Share Your Life Message\r\n5 Ways Pain Can Be Used for God\r\n•	To draw closer to God\r\n•	To draw closer to Others\r\n•	To become more like Jesus\r\n•	To help Others\r\n•	To witness to the World\r\n4 Types of Care Group of Fellowship\r\n•	1st Level (Shallow/Surface Level) - Fellowship of Sharing\r\n•	2nd Level - Fellowship of Studying\r\n•	3rd Level - Fellowship of Serving\r\n•	4th Level (Deepest, Most Vulnerable Level) - Fellowship of Suffering',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05'),
(42927,	273,	9247,	'On a personal level, to carry on doing the right thing even though suffering, to not use that as a crutch. On a ministry level, to look into developing the depth of fellowship among our care group.',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05'),
(42928,	273,	9248,	'Really grateful for this series, was a real eye-opener to some of my blindspots, especially in regards to grieving.',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05',	'2017-11-18 14:33:05'),
(42929,	4218,	31,	'obedience really is a form of worship\r\nworship is not about singing songs,its about being obedient\r\nbeing more aware of God\'s word on obedience',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46'),
(42930,	4218,	32,	'think before i leap',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46'),
(42931,	4218,	33,	'eye opening!',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46',	'2017-11-18 17:47:46'),
(42932,	4223,	1,	'It is impossible to view kingdom principles with a democratic mindset\r\nThere is freedom in submission, there is bondage in rebellion\r\nToo many see themselves only accounted for by God',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00'),
(42933,	4223,	2,	'Not to allow myself to become divided.  To make sure any vision I have is inline with God’s vision.',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00'),
(42934,	4223,	3,	'I feel that being a state trooper has helped to prepare me and better understand authority and submission.',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00',	'2017-11-18 18:39:00'),
